1
00:02:04,090 --> 00:02:08,120
No living creature was harmed during
the filming of this series.

2
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:23,880
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:02:24,740 --> 00:02:26,060
Osman Bey.

4
00:02:27,350 --> 00:02:28,240
Stop.

5
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:32,790
I'm here on behalf of the Emperor.

6
00:02:34,110 --> 00:02:36,690
You are fighting the wrong enemy.

7
00:02:52,750 --> 00:02:54,950
I don't know with whom you work but...

8
00:02:57,370 --> 00:02:59,720
we are not leaving here.

9
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:05,540
Allow me to explain to you.

10
00:03:08,970 --> 00:03:10,660
Your son, Alaaddin...

11
00:03:11,050 --> 00:03:13,380
is captured by Emperor's enemies.

12
00:03:17,890 --> 00:03:20,110
What are you saying?

13
00:03:25,420 --> 00:03:27,470
What are you saying?

14
00:03:30,970 --> 00:03:32,930
Enemies have entered our home.

15
00:03:32,970 --> 00:03:35,080
How do you guard this door?

16
00:03:35,170 --> 00:03:36,330
Are you blind?

17
00:03:36,900 --> 00:03:38,750
Are you deaf?

18
00:03:39,250 --> 00:03:42,420
Answer me, Alps!

19
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:46,350
- Who am I talking to?
- Bala Hatun.

20
00:03:47,310 --> 00:03:48,550
Who am I talking to?

21
00:03:48,590 --> 00:03:49,930
Answer me.

22
00:03:49,970 --> 00:03:50,850
Bala Hatun.

23
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:55,820
Patience, Bala Hatun.

24
00:03:56,170 --> 00:03:57,980
This is not the time to be angry.

25
00:03:58,900 --> 00:04:02,880
Allah will surely help you.

26
00:04:06,450 --> 00:04:08,080
We will find Alaaddin.

27
00:04:10,980 --> 00:04:11,980
Aktemur

28
00:04:13,519 --> 00:04:14,820
Is there a trace?

29
00:04:15,750 --> 00:04:17,269
There are wheel traces.

30
00:04:17,290 --> 00:04:18,820
However, there are
no traces ahead.

31
00:04:18,839 --> 00:04:19,850
We have to trace it.

32
00:04:19,890 --> 00:04:21,240
Let's go now.

33
00:04:21,339 --> 00:04:22,280
Alps!

34
00:04:22,390 --> 00:04:24,040
Get the horses ready!

35
00:04:25,230 --> 00:04:26,800
Dursun Fakı.

36
00:04:31,290 --> 00:04:32,980
Be careful.

37
00:04:33,380 --> 00:04:40,320
Aladdin Ali, I will kill the ones
who uprooted you from your branch.

38
00:04:41,810 --> 00:04:42,550
Who?

39
00:04:43,810 --> 00:04:45,280
Who did this?

40
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:47,890
The ones who wanted to kill the emperor.

41
00:04:51,030 --> 00:04:51,990
Ophelia.

42
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:56,280
Emperor's daughter.

43
00:05:00,170 --> 00:05:01,940
But Ophelia is not alone.

44
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:06,680
Frigg, who is sent to this
country to destroy you...

45
00:05:11,390 --> 00:05:13,650
These are our enemies, Osman Bey.

46
00:05:13,950 --> 00:05:15,930
There is no such thing as "we".

47
00:05:18,810 --> 00:05:20,820
You are on the side.

48
00:05:21,900 --> 00:05:23,240
We are on the other side.

49
00:05:24,030 --> 00:05:27,840
You had their enmity that day by
saving Constantinople.

50
00:05:28,650 --> 00:05:32,310
If the enemy is one, then we
are one too, Osman Bey.

51
00:05:33,170 --> 00:05:34,630
And that dog?

52
00:05:35,260 --> 00:05:38,110
He is Olof, the most respected
warrior of Rome.

53
00:05:40,790 --> 00:05:44,940
He wanted to avenge for
Öktem Bey's massacre in the village.

54
00:05:46,770 --> 00:05:47,770
It's wrong.

55
00:05:49,850 --> 00:05:51,270
Kantakuzenos.

56
00:05:54,540 --> 00:05:57,730
If my son is hurt...

57
00:06:02,500 --> 00:06:04,700
I will kill you all.

58
00:06:09,930 --> 00:06:13,120
If I had been afraid of this, I wouldn't
have come with a few men.

59
00:06:14,860 --> 00:06:17,270
I trust your friendship.

60
00:06:18,910 --> 00:06:22,960
I believe we will destroy the game
those two demons created.

61
00:06:24,760 --> 00:06:27,230
How did you know all these things?

62
00:06:28,440 --> 00:06:30,910
I've been after them since that dark day.

63
00:06:31,610 --> 00:06:33,770
I caught one of Frigg's men.

64
00:06:34,110 --> 00:06:36,590
And it brought me to these places.

65
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:50,490
If you're lying...

66
00:06:53,290 --> 00:06:57,510
I'll wrap that rope around
your neck with my hands.

67
00:07:02,460 --> 00:07:04,000
Where is the man?

68
00:07:05,280 --> 00:07:06,840
Underground.

69
00:07:06,910 --> 00:07:08,600
Kantakuzenos.

70
00:07:11,300 --> 00:07:12,390
Olof...

71
00:07:14,070 --> 00:07:16,210
killed my Alps

72
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:18,460
and blamed them.

73
00:07:21,480 --> 00:07:24,750
And you came to tell me about the
witness of a death.

74
00:07:24,900 --> 00:07:27,260
How long do you allow
traitors to survive?

75
00:07:27,620 --> 00:07:29,500
Or those who attacked the village?

76
00:07:34,290 --> 00:07:36,110
Why did they kidnap my son?

77
00:07:36,600 --> 00:07:38,490
They kidnapped him for Dan.

78
00:07:40,220 --> 00:07:41,610
Dan is Frigg's brother.

79
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:44,860
Loyal maid of Ophelia.

80
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:49,350
Constantinople
Emperor's Palace

81
00:07:51,340 --> 00:07:54,080
My beloved daughter, Ophelia.

82
00:07:54,450 --> 00:07:57,830
She made a light and sturdy shield for me.

83
00:07:58,170 --> 00:08:02,240
No harm will come
to you, Honorable Emperor.

84
00:08:03,080 --> 00:08:05,740
That's why Kantakuzenos
asked me to stay by your side.

85
00:08:05,850 --> 00:08:09,550
So, Kantakozanos loves me like Ophelia.

86
00:08:29,580 --> 00:08:30,929
Are you okay, sir?

87
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:33,520
Yes.

88
00:08:34,710 --> 00:08:37,549
There must have been a
needle left while making the shield.

89
00:08:37,780 --> 00:08:39,049
How is that possible?

90
00:08:39,210 --> 00:08:42,299
Princess Ophelia has acted with caution.

91
00:08:47,790 --> 00:08:48,810
My Father

92
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:53,750
You tried the shield then

93
00:08:56,240 --> 00:08:57,060
My father.

94
00:08:59,050 --> 00:09:00,540
Father!

95
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:01,880
- Father!
- Stop it!

96
00:09:02,220 --> 00:09:03,640
Stop, don't come close.

97
00:09:04,100 --> 00:09:05,860
The shield may
be poisoned.

98
00:09:06,170 --> 00:09:09,150
Hey, call the doctor quickly.

99
00:09:10,090 --> 00:09:11,080
My Father.

100
00:09:11,290 --> 00:09:12,490
Emperor!

101
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:21,660
Tell me everything.

102
00:09:23,810 --> 00:09:25,520
Tell me everything.

103
00:09:25,690 --> 00:09:28,750
This poison will slowly kill you.

104
00:09:47,340 --> 00:09:49,090
You are the person closest to him.

105
00:09:49,300 --> 00:09:50,980
You brought the shield.

106
00:09:54,690 --> 00:09:55,740
Soldiers.

107
00:09:56,480 --> 00:09:58,070
Arrest the princess.

108
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:08,980
You fools, what are you waiting for?

109
00:10:24,660 --> 00:10:26,660
I will take my son from their hands.

110
00:10:27,210 --> 00:10:33,050
But if it turns out that you are
responsible for these...

111
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:35,380
I did not do anything.

112
00:10:36,140 --> 00:10:39,140
I am your friend who stands
tall in front of you.

113
00:10:43,040 --> 00:10:44,720
I will accept your words now.

114
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:47,290
However, Olof...

115
00:10:48,710 --> 00:10:51,850
He will be punished for
what he did to my Alps.

116
00:10:52,330 --> 00:10:56,880
If Öktem is punished for
destroying the village...

117
00:10:57,810 --> 00:11:00,110
I will pay for every drop of blood I shed.

118
00:11:00,580 --> 00:11:02,390
Don't worry, Olof.

119
00:11:02,850 --> 00:11:05,390
When the time comes, you will
pay that price...

120
00:11:05,820 --> 00:11:08,030
Respected warrior of Rome.

121
00:11:12,660 --> 00:11:15,600
We are very clear, Osman
Bey, as you have seen.

122
00:11:16,220 --> 00:11:19,070
If you want, let's talk about what
we're going to do next.

123
00:11:41,610 --> 00:11:43,320
We'll talk.

124
00:11:45,330 --> 00:11:46,980
We'll talk.

125
00:12:09,610 --> 00:12:11,700
You can't go back, Osman.

126
00:12:23,100 --> 00:12:25,190
Have mercy on me, my God...

127
00:12:25,410 --> 00:12:27,450
and protect my father.

128
00:12:43,870 --> 00:12:45,780
Break the door.

129
00:12:47,670 --> 00:12:49,270
Search!

130
00:12:50,530 --> 00:12:52,350
Look for her everywhere.

131
00:13:07,560 --> 00:13:09,720
How long can you escape?

132
00:13:10,870 --> 00:13:12,220
Princess.

133
00:13:20,660 --> 00:13:25,320
Osman fell for the trick and we will
wait.

134
00:13:27,020 --> 00:13:29,390
Tell me everything
before I kill you.

135
00:13:29,880 --> 00:13:31,100
Talk!

136
00:13:32,420 --> 00:13:35,600
You shouldn't do that, Olof.

137
00:13:37,110 --> 00:13:39,170
I faithfully executed the plan.

138
00:13:39,470 --> 00:13:42,440
Why didn't you allow me to
cut off Osman's head?

139
00:13:42,700 --> 00:13:44,200
Tell me.

140
00:13:48,370 --> 00:13:50,610
Frigg also agrees with me.

141
00:13:51,660 --> 00:13:54,020
She kidnapped Alaaddin for us.

142
00:14:05,280 --> 00:14:09,600
We can't destroy him like that, moreover,
this would be Dan's death decision.

143
00:14:10,370 --> 00:14:12,630
Do you want to lose another brother?

144
00:14:13,550 --> 00:14:18,210
I won't sacrifice another brother.

145
00:14:18,660 --> 00:14:20,960
Then we'll play this game
by my rules.

146
00:14:21,510 --> 00:14:24,930
Alaaddin is in our hands and
Osman will find him.

147
00:14:25,230 --> 00:14:27,020
But he won't get out of there alive.

148
00:14:27,890 --> 00:14:29,600
I will not barter.

149
00:14:30,130 --> 00:14:32,040
I will attack Yenişehir.

150
00:14:32,750 --> 00:14:34,360
and kill his son.

151
00:14:34,680 --> 00:14:36,830
Why are things so difficult, Olof?

152
00:14:37,640 --> 00:14:40,550
Osman will die anyway
while saving Alaaddin.

153
00:14:40,930 --> 00:14:43,850
And you will enter the city
quietly and take your brother.

154
00:14:44,360 --> 00:14:48,530
Then I will bring the Nicaea army and
destroy the city of Yenişehir.

155
00:14:52,660 --> 00:14:54,210
And then...

156
00:14:55,800 --> 00:15:01,170
You will return to Constantinople
as a hero.

157
00:15:01,670 --> 00:15:02,820
Not me...

158
00:15:03,850 --> 00:15:05,280
but us.

159
00:15:08,480 --> 00:15:12,180
And after I sit on the throne, we will
be hell for all the Turks.

160
00:15:13,580 --> 00:15:17,420
I support you because you
are valuable to me, Olof.

161
00:15:27,240 --> 00:15:30,370
I want to trust you, Kantakuzenos.

162
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:32,640
Be careful not to disappoint me.

163
00:15:37,140 --> 00:15:40,530
If you make a mistake, I will
cut off your head.

164
00:16:08,850 --> 00:16:11,110
Wheel tracks point to this point.

165
00:16:22,890 --> 00:16:23,890
Osman.

166
00:16:24,030 --> 00:16:26,190
Bala, what's happening?

167
00:16:31,180 --> 00:16:32,200
Osman.

168
00:16:32,780 --> 00:16:34,580
What happened?

169
00:16:34,810 --> 00:16:37,400
They kidnapped Alaaddin.

170
00:16:45,050 --> 00:16:48,270
But we found the tracks
of the wheels, my Bey.

171
00:16:57,410 --> 00:17:00,819
My Bey, the traces brought us here but...

172
00:17:01,190 --> 00:17:03,339
the road splits in two ways.

173
00:17:07,160 --> 00:17:13,180
I will kill
whoever did this to my son.

174
00:17:16,079 --> 00:17:18,220
So, Kantakuzenos was right.

175
00:17:21,410 --> 00:17:23,579
We will follow the tracks of the carriage.

176
00:17:24,119 --> 00:17:26,130
Half of the Alps will go from this side.

177
00:17:26,750 --> 00:17:30,260
Aktemur, you will go to the tribe of
Öktem Bey with Turgut Bey.

178
00:17:30,650 --> 00:17:32,630
You will bring the bodies of the martyrs.

179
00:17:33,050 --> 00:17:34,680
You will search the tribe.

180
00:17:34,750 --> 00:17:35,940
Your command, my Bey.

181
00:17:36,020 --> 00:17:37,060
Come on.

182
00:17:37,750 --> 00:17:39,760
And we'll go find our son, come on.

183
00:17:48,280 --> 00:17:49,340
Come on.

184
00:18:25,500 --> 00:18:27,570
Damn you, you little mouse!

185
00:18:32,120 --> 00:18:34,740
Kill me! Come on, what
are you waiting for?

186
00:18:34,890 --> 00:18:37,480
You will live for a while until we kill
your father.

187
00:18:37,800 --> 00:18:39,550
Then you will all die.

188
00:18:39,790 --> 00:18:42,390
I won't remain a prisoner in the
hands of the enemy...

189
00:18:42,420 --> 00:18:43,940
and my father won't fall into your trap.
Kill me!

190
00:18:53,540 --> 00:18:59,190
Today we will take our revenge on Osman.

191
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:02,240
For Valhalla!

192
00:19:02,450 --> 00:19:04,800
- For Valhalla!
- For Valhalla!

193
00:19:04,890 --> 00:19:07,490
- For Valhalla!
- For Valhalla!

194
00:19:07,660 --> 00:19:10,330
- For Valhalla!
- For Valhalla!

195
00:19:23,600 --> 00:19:26,050
I really like the fresh
fish you make, Leo.

196
00:19:26,680 --> 00:19:28,860
Let me taste it.

197
00:19:37,050 --> 00:19:38,910
Get ready, Leo!

198
00:19:39,530 --> 00:19:42,050
While Osman goes behind Alaaddin...

199
00:19:42,570 --> 00:19:46,250
we're going to rescue Dan from
the dungeon.

200
00:19:47,270 --> 00:19:49,960
The situation is complex
and Alps are everywhere.

201
00:19:50,230 --> 00:19:52,400
They close all the shops.

202
00:20:05,250 --> 00:20:08,500
I smell your fear, Leo, or are
you really afraid?

203
00:20:08,880 --> 00:20:11,980
No, I'm not afraid.

204
00:20:12,960 --> 00:20:15,160
When are we going to the dungeon?

205
00:20:16,040 --> 00:20:17,810
Don't be in a hurry, Leo.

206
00:20:18,170 --> 00:20:22,150
A big guest will come to Yenişehir, we
have to meet him first.

207
00:20:51,370 --> 00:20:52,980
Cerkutay.

208
00:20:55,630 --> 00:20:56,870
Alps!

209
00:21:28,260 --> 00:21:29,590
In the name of Allah.

210
00:21:39,265 --> 00:21:40,265
Don't come.

211
00:21:49,940 --> 00:21:51,610
The box is empty, my Bey.

212
00:22:07,770 --> 00:22:09,470
He wrote in his own blood, my Bey.

213
00:22:12,260 --> 00:22:14,010
He says "don't come."

214
00:22:16,660 --> 00:22:21,550
If they hurt my son, I won't let them rest in
this world and the hereafter, Osman.

215
00:22:21,810 --> 00:22:23,270
Don't worry, Bala.

216
00:22:23,910 --> 00:22:26,110
However, we should be careful.

217
00:22:27,380 --> 00:22:29,670
Our son has seen their trap.

218
00:22:38,260 --> 00:22:40,410
Now, listen to me well.

219
00:22:44,050 --> 00:22:46,420
I will try to be patient and tolerant...

220
00:22:48,510 --> 00:22:50,330
but what about the people?

221
00:22:54,100 --> 00:22:58,900
You should at least bring them the
corpses of their sons, Öktem Bey.

222
00:22:59,240 --> 00:23:01,880
What should I do, Hatun?

223
00:23:02,380 --> 00:23:04,740
The Sheikh restricted my movement.

224
00:23:06,350 --> 00:23:08,230
How can I get over his words?

225
00:23:08,540 --> 00:23:11,170
It is not permissible to ignore the
Sheikh's words.

226
00:23:11,920 --> 00:23:15,540
But if you object, they will think
that there is sedition.

227
00:23:18,570 --> 00:23:22,540
You didn't say that when you were
next to the Sheikh, Bayındır.

228
00:23:27,780 --> 00:23:30,470
I am willing to sacrifice
myself for you, Öktem Bey.

229
00:23:31,580 --> 00:23:34,980
However, you almost fought
the men of Osman Bey.

230
00:23:35,310 --> 00:23:38,480
The blood was going to be shed, so
I decided to act like this.

231
00:23:39,010 --> 00:23:43,410
It isn't appropriate for us to leave the bodies
of our martyrs in the hands of the infidels.

232
00:23:43,440 --> 00:23:45,010
This is it.

233
00:23:46,200 --> 00:23:47,780
Bayındır.

234
00:24:41,760 --> 00:24:43,200
Don't cover up, Bengi Hatun.

235
00:24:45,340 --> 00:24:46,990
They are not well.

236
00:24:52,880 --> 00:24:54,190
Don't do that, Hatun.

237
00:24:55,190 --> 00:24:56,190
Don't.

238
00:24:56,750 --> 00:25:01,220
You should've held the hands of the infidels
who killed these valiants, not mine.

239
00:25:02,720 --> 00:25:03,720
Now, let me.

240
00:25:03,990 --> 00:25:04,990
I will see them.

241
00:25:05,380 --> 00:25:06,700
Don't do that, Hatun.

242
00:25:06,880 --> 00:25:07,880
Don't.

243
00:25:10,370 --> 00:25:12,220
Go away, Öktem Bey.

244
00:25:12,950 --> 00:25:14,620
I will see them.

245
00:25:33,650 --> 00:25:34,650
Batur.

246
00:25:36,180 --> 00:25:37,180
Batur.

247
00:25:38,590 --> 00:25:40,030
I'm sorry.

248
00:25:42,140 --> 00:25:43,970
Thank you.

249
00:27:06,080 --> 00:27:07,170
Sarkis.

250
00:27:07,690 --> 00:27:09,500
God has sent you.

251
00:27:15,760 --> 00:27:16,760
From this direction.

252
00:27:25,110 --> 00:27:27,650
Messengers have come from
Constantinople, Ayşe Hatun.

253
00:27:27,660 --> 00:27:29,080
They want to see Osman Bey.

254
00:27:33,280 --> 00:27:34,570
Osman Bey isn't here.

255
00:27:35,970 --> 00:27:37,610
I'll let you meet Malhun Hatun.

256
00:27:39,040 --> 00:27:40,040
Please.

257
00:28:33,770 --> 00:28:36,650
Emperor Andronikos asked us to
deliver this to Osman Bey.

258
00:28:37,180 --> 00:28:39,290
He sent his regards to him.

259
00:28:55,160 --> 00:28:58,090
When Osman Bey comes, I
will give him.

260
00:28:58,600 --> 00:29:00,130
Now, you can go.

261
00:29:12,280 --> 00:29:13,750
Let it be good, Inshallah.

262
00:29:17,220 --> 00:29:20,210
When Osman Bey finds my dear Alaaddin
and bring him safely...

263
00:29:20,620 --> 00:29:23,440
we will know what the Emperor wants.

264
00:29:49,330 --> 00:29:50,330
Son.

265
00:30:01,770 --> 00:30:02,770
Oh my Allah.

266
00:30:10,090 --> 00:30:11,090
Aladdin!

267
00:30:15,880 --> 00:30:16,880
We got you.

268
00:30:20,130 --> 00:30:22,360
Aladdin, dear Aladdin.

269
00:30:25,900 --> 00:30:27,590
- Aladdin!
- Is he okay?

270
00:30:29,890 --> 00:30:31,950
- Father.
- Thank Allah.

271
00:30:32,890 --> 00:30:33,910
It's fine, it's fine.

272
00:30:34,380 --> 00:30:35,850
Come on, son.

273
00:30:40,780 --> 00:30:41,780
Come on.

274
00:30:42,050 --> 00:30:43,630
Aladdin, my son.

275
00:30:46,360 --> 00:30:47,360
Right now!

276
00:30:51,770 --> 00:30:52,770
Alps!

277
00:30:58,170 --> 00:31:00,390
You tried to take my son away from me.

278
00:31:00,530 --> 00:31:03,350
No power can take you out of my hands.

279
00:31:03,380 --> 00:31:04,380
Yes.

280
00:31:04,750 --> 00:31:05,750
Yes.

281
00:31:10,210 --> 00:31:13,500
Attack! Kill them all!

282
00:31:40,700 --> 00:31:41,700
Son.

283
00:31:42,890 --> 00:31:44,910
I took care of you like you
were my son.

284
00:31:46,310 --> 00:31:48,660
But I couldn't keep the promise
I made to my mom.

285
00:31:48,770 --> 00:31:49,770
Dear Batur.

286
00:31:53,500 --> 00:31:56,000
While I was saying I'm going to
have your wedding...

287
00:31:56,000 --> 00:31:58,470
and see you as a Bey...

288
00:32:00,290 --> 00:32:02,290
Now I will wrap you in a white shroud.

289
00:32:03,750 --> 00:32:05,020
Hatun.

290
00:32:05,560 --> 00:32:06,640
Don't cry.

291
00:32:08,710 --> 00:32:09,910
Batur became a martyr.

292
00:32:13,360 --> 00:32:15,060
We don't deserve to cry.

293
00:32:16,890 --> 00:32:18,050
No crying anymore.

294
00:32:24,340 --> 00:32:25,670
No crying.

295
00:32:28,130 --> 00:32:29,490
No crying anymore.

296
00:32:35,820 --> 00:32:37,050
It's revenge time.

297
00:32:43,290 --> 00:32:44,800
It's revenge time but...

298
00:32:46,820 --> 00:32:51,810
do you have the courage to hold Osman
accountable for this?

299
00:32:52,270 --> 00:32:53,270
Öktem Bey.

300
00:32:54,810 --> 00:32:56,190
If it wasn't for Osman...

301
00:32:57,800 --> 00:32:58,800
my brother..

302
00:32:59,770 --> 00:33:01,160
would be here and alive now.

303
00:33:04,480 --> 00:33:06,790
Osman is the one who
caused my brother's death.

304
00:33:08,050 --> 00:33:10,090
What is Osman's fault?

305
00:33:11,130 --> 00:33:13,770
If you are looking for the guilty
then I am here woman.

306
00:33:15,040 --> 00:33:17,710
I'm the one who sent him
to the border.

307
00:33:18,690 --> 00:33:21,050
I'm the one who sent him, Hatun.

308
00:33:21,100 --> 00:33:22,910
Open your eyes, Öktem Bey!

309
00:33:23,730 --> 00:33:24,730
Open!

310
00:33:26,060 --> 00:33:28,450
You still trust Osman.

311
00:33:29,420 --> 00:33:30,870
See the truth, please.

312
00:33:32,100 --> 00:33:33,930
Osman is the only culprit.

313
00:33:35,690 --> 00:33:38,830
This happened to us because he
makes agreements with the infidels.

314
00:33:39,480 --> 00:33:42,800
You weren't allowed to take Alps
but Turgut went and took them.

315
00:33:43,800 --> 00:33:46,960
He will stop our revenge.

316
00:33:49,220 --> 00:33:51,680
And our blood will be left on the ground.

317
00:33:52,450 --> 00:33:54,010
Not just this.

318
00:33:54,900 --> 00:33:58,010
They will want to kill you, Öktem Bey!

319
00:33:59,590 --> 00:34:03,949
They want your
soul and your position.

320
00:34:05,110 --> 00:34:06,610
Hatun...

321
00:34:07,440 --> 00:34:09,030
I don't fear death.

322
00:34:10,100 --> 00:34:12,728
My place is known...

323
00:34:13,300 --> 00:34:14,810
and my tribe is well known.

324
00:34:16,150 --> 00:34:19,040
Let him come and kill me if he dares.

325
00:34:19,380 --> 00:34:21,870
Don't say that, Öktem Bey.

326
00:34:22,710 --> 00:34:25,150
This is not a brave war, don't you see?

327
00:34:26,260 --> 00:34:27,719
They will betray you.

328
00:34:29,150 --> 00:34:32,560
They will make agreements with the
infidels and trick us.

329
00:34:33,110 --> 00:34:34,659
They brought our martyrs.

330
00:34:34,800 --> 00:34:38,409
Why does Turgut Bey stay here?
Why doesn't he go?

331
00:34:38,500 --> 00:34:41,030
Will they put a guard on us, Öktem Bey?

332
00:34:41,070 --> 00:34:43,449
Don't give in to your
anger, don't do this.

333
00:34:44,300 --> 00:34:45,760
I tell you we have martyrs.

334
00:34:46,920 --> 00:34:51,310
This isn't the right time
to talk about this, Hatun.

335
00:34:56,159 --> 00:34:58,920
- From now on...
- There will be no more than this!

336
00:34:59,810 --> 00:35:02,190
I'll bury my brother...

337
00:35:06,160 --> 00:35:07,160
but I will not bury you.

338
00:35:08,110 --> 00:35:11,080
Öktem Bey, I will not put
you under the soil.

339
00:35:12,150 --> 00:35:14,630
Despite you, I won't.

340
00:35:16,380 --> 00:35:23,330
If I must disobey your order to protect you, I will, Öktem Bey!

341
00:35:23,590 --> 00:35:24,770
You should know that.

342
00:35:25,360 --> 00:35:27,190
Don't say that, Hatun.

343
00:35:29,050 --> 00:35:30,570
Mother. Father.

344
00:35:31,800 --> 00:35:32,800
Don't do this.

345
00:35:35,180 --> 00:35:37,020
Let's do our last duty for
my uncle.

346
00:35:37,320 --> 00:35:39,960
You're right my daughter, let's do it.

347
00:35:43,510 --> 00:35:44,510
Alps!

348
00:35:54,530 --> 00:35:55,700
Come on.

349
00:35:56,580 --> 00:35:57,760
Take out my son.

350
00:36:22,350 --> 00:36:25,010
They won't stop.

351
00:36:26,580 --> 00:36:29,780
They will cause us many misfortunes.

352
00:36:30,190 --> 00:36:32,810
Yenişehir

353
00:36:33,100 --> 00:36:35,720
Your girls have done well, my love.

354
00:36:37,190 --> 00:36:39,810
Do you think they have another option?

355
00:36:41,790 --> 00:36:43,220
This is our play area.

356
00:36:44,040 --> 00:36:45,860
Leo works as much as girls.

357
00:36:46,570 --> 00:36:49,190
He brought the prison
(dungeon) map.

358
00:36:49,570 --> 00:36:50,810
They're keeping Dan here.

359
00:36:53,620 --> 00:36:56,470
There are many men here.

360
00:36:56,940 --> 00:36:58,500
Cowards.

361
00:37:01,830 --> 00:37:04,540
Then, we will burn the whole city.

362
00:37:37,520 --> 00:37:41,450
Or we'll make some of them sleep.

363
00:37:42,420 --> 00:37:43,600
Understood.

364
00:37:44,740 --> 00:37:48,010
That's why you switched torches in prison.

365
00:37:49,360 --> 00:37:50,720
You are...

366
00:37:53,070 --> 00:37:56,070
my biggest strength, Frigg.

367
00:37:57,230 --> 00:37:58,230
Together...

368
00:37:59,800 --> 00:38:01,360
We are strong together.

369
00:38:30,720 --> 00:38:32,100
What is happening to us?

370
00:38:32,260 --> 00:38:33,290
Alps!

371
00:38:33,320 --> 00:38:34,570
There is an intrusion.

372
00:38:58,960 --> 00:39:00,730
Olof.

373
00:39:01,550 --> 00:39:03,180
So, you came.

374
00:39:28,060 --> 00:39:29,120
Come on, Bala.

375
00:39:29,280 --> 00:39:30,340
Alaaddin.

376
00:39:39,230 --> 00:39:40,430
it's our turn.

377
00:39:40,520 --> 00:39:42,590
They will stop where we want, my Bey.

378
00:39:43,260 --> 00:39:44,730
Alps!

379
00:39:44,795 --> 00:39:45,795
Back off!

380
00:39:48,800 --> 00:39:49,600
Archers.

381
00:39:53,010 --> 00:39:54,740
Armor wall!

382
00:39:54,850 --> 00:39:56,710
O, Allah!

383
00:39:57,470 --> 00:39:59,850
O, Allah!

384
00:40:00,200 --> 00:40:02,730
O, Allah!

385
00:40:06,250 --> 00:40:08,260
O, Allah!

386
00:40:08,540 --> 00:40:09,880
O, Allah!

387
00:40:10,040 --> 00:40:11,520
O, Allah!

388
00:40:43,870 --> 00:40:47,720
I admire your intelligence so much, my love.

389
00:40:49,560 --> 00:40:50,520
I know.

390
00:40:56,620 --> 00:40:57,810
My love.

391
00:40:58,930 --> 00:41:01,230
Do you smell death?

392
00:41:12,560 --> 00:41:13,480
Dan.

393
00:41:15,390 --> 00:41:16,250
Brother.

394
00:41:45,440 --> 00:41:48,050
Dan, my brother.

395
00:41:51,170 --> 00:41:54,620
Osman, I'll make you pay for this!

396
00:41:58,690 --> 00:42:01,340
I will flay your skin while
you are alive, Osman!

397
00:42:02,980 --> 00:42:04,880
Dan!

398
00:42:07,970 --> 00:42:09,610
Olof.

399
00:42:10,300 --> 00:42:12,260
I knew you would come.

400
00:42:13,160 --> 00:42:15,810
It doesn't matter.

401
00:42:19,440 --> 00:42:21,540
Osman will pay for this.

402
00:42:21,830 --> 00:42:22,550
Come on.

403
00:42:23,050 --> 00:42:24,260
Faster.

404
00:42:24,820 --> 00:42:26,210
The guards are waking up.

405
00:42:35,360 --> 00:42:36,890
Be careful, Alps!

406
00:42:45,380 --> 00:42:46,740
Kill them!

407
00:42:56,710 --> 00:42:59,030
There is an infiltration, Alps!

408
00:43:05,680 --> 00:43:08,290
Close the doors, Alps!

409
00:43:08,990 --> 00:43:11,180
Don't let them escape.

410
00:43:49,880 --> 00:43:52,580
- It's explosives.
- Careful, Ayşe.

411
00:43:53,930 --> 00:43:55,610
Ayşe!

412
00:44:09,850 --> 00:44:11,490
They are running away, Ayşe.

413
00:44:11,600 --> 00:44:13,600
- Come on, come on!
- Ignobles!

414
00:45:00,630 --> 00:45:02,260
Oh God, what's going on?

415
00:45:02,330 --> 00:45:04,180
Protect us all, Jesus Christ.

416
00:45:13,510 --> 00:45:14,590
Oh, baby.

417
00:45:14,690 --> 00:45:16,500
Don't be afraid, I'm on your side.

418
00:45:17,360 --> 00:45:19,990
Do not stay in the alleys, enter the
houses, there is infiltration.

419
00:45:30,020 --> 00:45:31,730
This way, Alps!

420
00:45:43,460 --> 00:45:45,830
Alps! Catch them.

421
00:45:45,930 --> 00:45:47,540
Go after them!

422
00:45:47,620 --> 00:45:49,960
Run, run!

423
00:45:52,130 --> 00:45:53,410
Run!

424
00:46:06,310 --> 00:46:08,110
Hold on, Alaaddin.

425
00:46:08,670 --> 00:46:09,990
My son, hold on.

426
00:46:12,360 --> 00:46:14,500
Come on, come on, come on.

427
00:46:14,660 --> 00:46:16,130
Sit down.

428
00:46:16,330 --> 00:46:17,550
Sit here.

429
00:46:17,740 --> 00:46:19,070
Sit down, son.

430
00:46:22,070 --> 00:46:24,290
You came out alive
out of forty people.

431
00:46:24,460 --> 00:46:26,010
Is there anyone braver than you?

432
00:46:27,620 --> 00:46:29,470
Thank Allah.

433
00:46:29,800 --> 00:46:31,900
You're fine son, you're fine.

434
00:46:34,360 --> 00:46:36,590
- Father.
- Yes.

435
00:46:37,630 --> 00:46:39,060
It was because of me.

436
00:46:39,200 --> 00:46:41,890
No, no.

437
00:46:41,890 --> 00:46:42,780
Alps!

438
00:46:43,200 --> 00:46:44,630
Give him water.

439
00:46:49,040 --> 00:46:50,620
Open your mouth.

440
00:46:50,990 --> 00:46:52,330
Drink, drink.

441
00:46:55,280 --> 00:46:56,250
You are fine.

442
00:47:02,220 --> 00:47:04,650
You saved us from the trap
with what you wrote.

443
00:47:16,250 --> 00:47:17,900
They are coming, my Bey.

444
00:47:19,000 --> 00:47:21,430
Come on, come on.

445
00:47:21,800 --> 00:47:23,150
Come on, son.

446
00:47:24,080 --> 00:47:25,190
Hold on.

447
00:47:25,420 --> 00:47:26,940
I will, father.

448
00:47:28,260 --> 00:47:29,240
Come on, Bala.

449
00:47:29,680 --> 00:47:31,530
Come on, Alps!

450
00:47:31,720 --> 00:47:33,650
Everyone knows their job.

451
00:47:45,290 --> 00:47:46,500
Ayşe.

452
00:47:47,530 --> 00:47:49,320
We couldn't catch up, Malhun.

453
00:47:49,930 --> 00:47:52,050
The prisoners and the man
with them escaped.

454
00:47:52,070 --> 00:47:53,970
And I sent our Alps after them.

455
00:47:54,150 --> 00:47:55,960
We will catch
them, Inshallah.

456
00:47:56,610 --> 00:47:57,970
They escaped.

457
00:47:58,130 --> 00:48:00,820
But there are still two
people inside, Ayşe.

458
00:48:01,410 --> 00:48:02,490
Alps!

459
00:48:02,790 --> 00:48:05,620
We are looking for two
people, a man and a woman.

460
00:48:05,790 --> 00:48:08,630
The woman was hiding her
face, it's hard to find her but...

461
00:48:08,730 --> 00:48:11,440
the man is injured.

462
00:48:11,590 --> 00:48:14,350
Do what you have to do
and find them, Ayşe.

463
00:48:14,610 --> 00:48:15,610
We will find them.

464
00:48:15,660 --> 00:48:18,610
Come on, Alps! Come on.

465
00:48:36,760 --> 00:48:37,860
Fool.

466
00:48:38,490 --> 00:48:39,600
You're injured.

467
00:48:39,820 --> 00:48:42,710
How do you come here when
you are in this situation? Say it.

468
00:48:42,730 --> 00:48:44,270
Did you leave a trace behind?

469
00:48:44,470 --> 00:48:45,550
No.

470
00:48:51,280 --> 00:48:52,800
You idiot.

471
00:48:53,190 --> 00:48:55,130
I won't let you spoil my game.

472
00:48:55,240 --> 00:48:57,180
You can't kill me, Frigg.

473
00:48:59,550 --> 00:49:01,590
I can.

474
00:49:31,580 --> 00:49:33,530
Hello?

475
00:49:36,180 --> 00:49:38,810
Martha, Mr. Leo.

476
00:49:41,320 --> 00:49:42,810
Hello?

477
00:49:45,700 --> 00:49:46,860
Martha.

478
00:49:47,040 --> 00:49:48,110
Malhun Hatun.

479
00:49:48,770 --> 00:49:49,940
Welcome.

480
00:49:51,960 --> 00:49:53,460
Please, don't bother me.

481
00:49:56,450 --> 00:49:57,980
It's inattention.

482
00:50:01,130 --> 00:50:03,180
What happened to
your hand, Martha?

483
00:50:03,580 --> 00:50:05,140
The screw in the fabric box.

484
00:50:06,010 --> 00:50:09,860
When I saw the silk, I didn't
notice the nail.

485
00:50:19,430 --> 00:50:20,660
What is that sound?

486
00:50:22,390 --> 00:50:24,230
They must be the little guests.

487
00:50:26,110 --> 00:50:27,460
Mice.

488
00:50:28,320 --> 00:50:29,610
It must be mice.

489
00:50:30,220 --> 00:50:32,960
How does a small mouse
make this sound?

490
00:50:36,370 --> 00:50:38,880
Not one, but there are three.

491
00:50:40,390 --> 00:50:41,990
However, one of them is dead.

492
00:50:44,640 --> 00:50:47,490
But the two are still alive.

493
00:50:50,840 --> 00:50:52,310
It's there.

494
00:51:07,970 --> 00:51:11,000
Malhun, the Alps in prison woke up.

495
00:51:16,260 --> 00:51:17,590
Tell Mr. Leo...

496
00:51:17,650 --> 00:51:19,650
to get rid of all mice.

497
00:51:19,830 --> 00:51:21,400
And you be careful.

498
00:51:22,900 --> 00:51:25,000
Show your hand to the doctor.

499
00:51:32,210 --> 00:51:33,610
You would ruin everything.

500
00:51:34,250 --> 00:51:35,490
You clumsy freak.

501
00:51:37,340 --> 00:51:39,640
"Show your hand to the doctor."

502
00:51:55,930 --> 00:51:57,250
Batur.

503
00:51:57,940 --> 00:51:59,990
My mother's memory.

504
00:52:00,110 --> 00:52:01,200
My brother.

505
00:52:02,680 --> 00:52:04,580
You were martyred but...

506
00:52:06,210 --> 00:52:09,880
your sister is in pain.

507
00:52:11,320 --> 00:52:12,640
My valiant.

508
00:52:15,220 --> 00:52:16,350
Öktem Bey.

509
00:52:17,470 --> 00:52:18,400
I know...

510
00:52:18,940 --> 00:52:20,800
we just buried your brother...

511
00:52:20,870 --> 00:52:22,350
and your pain is recent...

512
00:52:23,150 --> 00:52:25,880
But for the sake of those who
remained in the tribe...

513
00:52:27,130 --> 00:52:28,980
I have a job that can't wait.

514
00:52:29,170 --> 00:52:30,880
On such a sad day...

515
00:52:31,520 --> 00:52:34,630
What is the task that
can not wait, Turgut Bey?

516
00:52:39,700 --> 00:52:41,130
I will search your tribe.

517
00:52:45,760 --> 00:52:49,770
What is left in our tribe but
bereaved mothers?

518
00:52:50,800 --> 00:52:51,940
What are you going to look for?

519
00:52:52,110 --> 00:52:54,820
Taxes from Constantinople
to Macri are missing.

520
00:52:56,150 --> 00:52:58,950
Kantakuzenos thinks you have gold.

521
00:53:00,030 --> 00:53:01,950
My job is to find them.

522
00:53:02,220 --> 00:53:08,280
Will you look for the gold of Rome in a
Turkish tribe with a word from the infidel?

523
00:53:09,250 --> 00:53:10,710
Turgut Bey?

524
00:53:12,300 --> 00:53:13,750
Turgut Bey.

525
00:53:14,970 --> 00:53:18,470
You say Batur Alp stole
Macri's taxes, right?

526
00:53:18,970 --> 00:53:22,450
Nothing like this could ever
happen, it's impossible.

527
00:53:24,750 --> 00:53:28,710
I buried my brother's body in the grave.

528
00:53:29,250 --> 00:53:31,370
What are you saying, Turgut Bey?

529
00:53:31,470 --> 00:53:32,670
I say...

530
00:53:33,170 --> 00:53:36,250
Let's prevent the slander that
they accuse our martyrs with.

531
00:53:36,530 --> 00:53:38,310
Let us do our job.

532
00:53:38,970 --> 00:53:41,030
Let's get rid of that accusation.

533
00:53:42,340 --> 00:53:43,860
Stop, Hatun.
Stop.

534
00:53:49,730 --> 00:53:52,290
You are searching for the truth.

535
00:53:55,140 --> 00:53:57,370
We know the truth.

536
00:53:58,740 --> 00:54:00,500
Do your job.

537
00:54:01,540 --> 00:54:04,770
A slander only embarrasses its owner.

538
00:54:06,620 --> 00:54:07,570
Well.

539
00:54:09,820 --> 00:54:10,940
Aktemur.

540
00:54:12,820 --> 00:54:13,770
Alps.

541
00:54:34,820 --> 00:54:37,510
How much do the infidels pay
for each person, Hüseyin?

542
00:54:37,800 --> 00:54:40,650
I don't know, my Bey. They must have
taken 10 bags of gold.

543
00:54:40,740 --> 00:54:43,510
What ruthless infidels they are.

544
00:54:44,250 --> 00:54:46,450
Osman does not take a quarter of this.

545
00:54:47,480 --> 00:54:50,820
So, the tax of the village...

546
00:54:51,740 --> 00:54:54,770
is more than a chest of gold.

547
00:54:55,910 --> 00:54:57,370
A big chest of gold.

548
00:54:58,370 --> 00:54:59,370
Shiny.

549
00:55:00,480 --> 00:55:02,140
I say gold, Hüseyin.

550
00:55:03,850 --> 00:55:04,810
Look.

551
00:55:04,860 --> 00:55:05,770
Yes, my Bey.

552
00:55:08,020 --> 00:55:11,910
If Öktem really did this...

553
00:55:13,250 --> 00:55:15,140
the gold must be in this tribe.

554
00:55:15,800 --> 00:55:18,560
And if they tricked Öktem...

555
00:55:18,740 --> 00:55:20,560
the gold must be in this tribe anyway.

556
00:55:20,620 --> 00:55:22,620
It is true what you are saying, my Bey.

557
00:55:23,200 --> 00:55:26,250
How dare you confirm my words?

558
00:55:32,880 --> 00:55:34,740
Spread your Alps everywhere.

559
00:55:36,200 --> 00:55:39,050
Find the gold for me, Hüseyin.

560
00:55:39,450 --> 00:55:44,170
So that I can make you a Bey.

561
00:55:46,650 --> 00:55:50,080
What happened, Hüseyin? You
froze when you heard about gold.

562
00:55:51,140 --> 00:55:54,480
We will send a messenger to Sencer Bey.

563
00:55:55,940 --> 00:55:58,660
You mean Sencer, the brother-in-law of
the Sultan, right?

564
00:55:58,730 --> 00:56:00,510
Yeah, who did you think?

565
00:56:00,640 --> 00:56:03,180
Come on, write what I say.

566
00:56:11,540 --> 00:56:13,680
The Honorable Sencer Bey.

567
00:56:16,220 --> 00:56:18,970
As you know, Osman is a reckless person.

568
00:56:20,140 --> 00:56:23,140
He burned the lands and turned them
into ashes.

569
00:56:24,680 --> 00:56:26,740
He totally destroyed it.

570
00:56:26,850 --> 00:56:31,740
Othman is dragged into a war.

571
00:56:32,080 --> 00:56:38,000
This war will make us control the trade.

572
00:56:40,940 --> 00:56:43,230
Hold on, son.

573
00:56:43,340 --> 00:56:45,220
Hold on.

574
00:56:45,340 --> 00:56:46,370
Hold on, son.

575
00:56:47,240 --> 00:56:48,380
Hold on.

576
00:56:48,460 --> 00:56:49,660
Hold on.

577
00:56:50,370 --> 00:56:53,000
You are the hero today.

578
00:56:56,310 --> 00:56:57,600
My son.

579
00:56:58,540 --> 00:56:59,700
Son.

580
00:56:59,770 --> 00:57:01,000
My father.

581
00:57:04,880 --> 00:57:06,110
Come on.

582
00:57:06,450 --> 00:57:07,540
come up.

583
00:57:08,140 --> 00:57:09,220
Hold on.

584
00:57:13,290 --> 00:57:14,610
Come on, come on.

585
00:57:39,200 --> 00:57:40,620
Come on, Alps.

586
00:57:44,970 --> 00:57:46,420
Stop.

587
00:57:53,970 --> 00:57:55,410
Hold on, my son.

588
00:57:55,530 --> 00:57:56,920
Hold on.

589
00:57:59,360 --> 00:58:01,880
You can't escape from your end, Osman.

590
00:58:03,770 --> 00:58:06,320
You also won't run away.

591
00:58:06,570 --> 00:58:07,290
Alps!

592
00:58:09,340 --> 00:58:10,090
Boran.

593
00:58:17,310 --> 00:58:18,540
Ayaz!

594
00:58:21,680 --> 00:58:23,140
Shields!

595
00:58:25,230 --> 00:58:26,040
O Allah!

596
00:58:27,850 --> 00:58:29,200
Dumrul.

597
00:58:39,940 --> 00:58:42,310
The fire will be the end of you.

598
00:58:43,110 --> 00:58:46,310
People who are so skilled to
kidnap my son from Yenişehir...

599
00:58:46,740 --> 00:58:49,340
won't leave traces like this behind.

600
00:58:52,160 --> 00:58:54,060
The enemy is a new.

601
00:58:54,540 --> 00:58:56,430
But they are all the same.

602
00:58:56,600 --> 00:58:58,600
What shall we do then, my Bey?

603
00:58:59,620 --> 00:59:02,900
As long as they set a trap
for us by leaving traces...

604
00:59:03,080 --> 00:59:05,310
we will set a trap for them.

605
00:59:06,000 --> 00:59:09,280
We will act exactly like them.

606
00:59:09,450 --> 00:59:10,610
We will retreat.

607
00:59:13,010 --> 00:59:15,850
The war will happen where we want it.

608
00:59:16,230 --> 00:59:18,230
Not only this.

609
00:59:18,540 --> 00:59:22,880
They'll erect a wall of shields and try
to withdraw when they fall into the trap.

610
00:59:23,620 --> 00:59:25,800
We won't be able to catch any of them.

611
00:59:26,500 --> 00:59:29,940
That is why we will press
them with arrows and attack them.

612
00:59:30,040 --> 00:59:32,510
Until we drag them to where we want.

613
00:59:32,540 --> 00:59:34,460
When they get there...

614
00:59:34,540 --> 00:59:37,000
The only thing they will
give is their life.

615
00:59:38,540 --> 00:59:39,940
Cerkutay.

616
00:59:41,250 --> 00:59:42,400
Tell Boran.

617
00:59:42,650 --> 00:59:44,400
Your order, my Bey.

618
00:59:49,370 --> 00:59:52,620
You will stop where we want.

619
00:59:53,850 --> 00:59:55,480
Allah is the greatest!

620
00:59:56,250 --> 00:59:57,480
O Allah!

621
00:59:58,820 --> 01:00:01,210
Ignite!

622
01:00:06,270 --> 01:00:07,760
The truth is Allah!

623
01:00:13,230 --> 01:00:15,180
We will not allow them, brothers.

624
01:00:19,870 --> 01:00:22,110
Fires don't catch easily.

625
01:00:23,790 --> 01:00:26,080
However, Cerkutay's lungs are strong.

626
01:00:30,220 --> 01:00:33,710
To the right, to the right!

627
01:00:34,010 --> 01:00:36,090
To the right.

628
01:00:37,610 --> 01:00:40,220
Remember Cerkutay!

629
01:00:40,840 --> 01:00:42,100
Cerkutay!

630
01:00:42,140 --> 01:00:44,540
Cerkutay never dies!

631
01:00:44,600 --> 01:00:46,000
Come on.

632
01:01:14,740 --> 01:01:16,460
The field became ours.

633
01:01:16,660 --> 01:01:19,000
Shoot the arrows of the Turks.

634
01:01:30,780 --> 01:01:32,290
Allah is eternal!

635
01:01:32,400 --> 01:01:34,140
Allah is the greatest!

636
01:01:34,280 --> 01:01:36,460
Allah is the greatest!

637
01:02:10,350 --> 01:02:12,410
You put your hand on my son.

638
01:02:13,160 --> 01:02:15,500
I will cut off your heads one by one.

639
01:02:16,190 --> 01:02:18,320
But now it's your turn.

640
01:02:36,270 --> 01:02:37,310
You can't enter.

641
01:02:37,680 --> 01:02:39,040
I don't allow it.

642
01:02:39,140 --> 01:02:41,290
Your words are valid in
Yenişehir, commander.

643
01:02:41,470 --> 01:02:43,020
Stick to your limits.

644
01:02:46,700 --> 01:02:49,530
The extent of my limits is beyond
your imagination, Hatun.

645
01:02:49,780 --> 01:02:52,020
Go away and let me do my job.

646
01:02:55,190 --> 01:02:58,040
My sword is sharper than
your dagger, you should know that.

647
01:02:58,090 --> 01:03:00,370
There is no turning back
on this, commander.

648
01:03:01,500 --> 01:03:03,160
Hatun.

649
01:03:03,390 --> 01:03:05,070
I told you to go away.

650
01:03:05,450 --> 01:03:07,640
This time
I won't be forgiving.

651
01:03:08,050 --> 01:03:10,060
There is no other way to reveal the truth.

652
01:03:14,510 --> 01:03:16,360
Can't you hear my words, Hatun?

653
01:03:17,930 --> 01:03:18,830
Alçiçek.

654
01:03:34,690 --> 01:03:36,050
Move, my daughter.

655
01:03:38,740 --> 01:03:40,280
Let them search.

656
01:03:41,120 --> 01:03:43,330
I have nothing to hide from anyone.

657
01:03:44,360 --> 01:03:48,240
I'm curious if they'll be able to
look at our faces after this.

658
01:03:49,840 --> 01:03:50,720
Go in and search.

659
01:03:51,130 --> 01:03:52,370
Father.

660
01:03:52,560 --> 01:03:53,750
Enter.

661
01:03:55,250 --> 01:03:57,280
Alps.

662
01:04:41,550 --> 01:04:42,280
Kutlu Alp.

663
01:04:45,390 --> 01:04:46,580
What's up, Kutlu Alp?

664
01:04:46,970 --> 01:04:49,890
We're looking but it looks like
there's nothing, my Bey.

665
01:04:50,850 --> 01:04:52,140
There is basically nothing.

666
01:04:52,170 --> 01:04:54,900
You are looking for
something that does not exist.

667
01:04:56,140 --> 01:05:00,140
Are you searching people's tents after
failing to find anything?

668
01:05:00,140 --> 01:05:00,150
Alcicek.
Are you searching people's tents after
failing to find anything?

669
01:05:00,150 --> 01:05:00,970
Alcicek.

670
01:05:01,950 --> 01:05:02,650
Hatun.

671
01:05:04,440 --> 01:05:05,720
I believe your words.

672
01:05:06,720 --> 01:05:08,510
And I know you don't have gold.

673
01:05:08,940 --> 01:05:10,510
Why are you searching then?

674
01:05:11,820 --> 01:05:13,400
Because it is a matter of state.

675
01:05:14,210 --> 01:05:15,230
It's my job.

676
01:05:15,730 --> 01:05:17,630
And I do what I have to do.

677
01:05:18,460 --> 01:05:20,240
If you trust my words...

678
01:05:20,690 --> 01:05:21,760
...just wait.

679
01:05:22,160 --> 01:05:25,760
The more we remain silent and wait
the more you accuse us, Subasi!

680
01:05:26,360 --> 01:05:29,400
Uncle, father and now this gold!

681
01:05:29,400 --> 01:05:31,430
It's one trouble after anoter, I know.

682
01:05:31,430 --> 01:05:32,550
I know that

683
01:05:33,400 --> 01:05:35,180
I know it's a tough situation.

684
01:05:35,560 --> 01:05:39,570
But I also know that
the brave Hatun who beat me in the duel...

685
01:05:40,420 --> 01:05:42,260
...must know how to deal with this.

686
01:05:42,670 --> 01:05:44,680
Don't remind me that, Subasi!

687
01:05:45,490 --> 01:05:47,490
It didn't end well for me.

688
01:05:49,440 --> 01:05:52,830
They say "every cloud has a silver lining"

689
01:05:53,930 --> 01:05:54,970
I know you.

690
01:05:57,090 --> 01:05:58,490
I know you.

691
01:05:59,300 --> 01:06:00,360
I saw you.

692
01:06:00,930 --> 01:06:03,030
I know you wouldn't do that.

693
01:06:03,970 --> 01:06:06,560
I and Osman Bey are on your side

694
01:06:11,090 --> 01:06:11,790
Alps!

695
01:06:12,580 --> 01:06:13,300
Gather up!

696
01:06:17,390 --> 01:06:19,290
My Bey, check it out!

697
01:06:35,300 --> 01:06:36,240
Alps!

698
01:06:36,240 --> 01:06:37,480
Come on

699
01:06:41,500 --> 01:06:42,780
You are wasting your time.

700
01:06:50,190 --> 01:06:51,870
Hurry up Alps!

701
01:07:05,150 --> 01:07:06,500
Come on, take it out!

702
01:07:27,080 --> 01:07:28,340
Get it out quickly!

703
01:07:38,450 --> 01:07:39,540
What is this?

704
01:07:39,690 --> 01:07:41,130
Is this Roman gold?

705
01:07:47,360 --> 01:07:48,890
Turgut Bey!

706
01:08:22,970 --> 01:08:24,880
This is not ours

707
01:08:25,410 --> 01:08:27,520
Look at that!

708
01:08:28,850 --> 01:08:29,800
Oktem Bey.

709
01:08:31,279 --> 01:08:33,300
We trust you and stand behind you.

710
01:08:34,620 --> 01:08:36,279
And is this what you do in return?

711
01:08:42,920 --> 01:08:44,198
In this case..

712
01:08:46,000 --> 01:08:47,390
It's over, Oktem Bey.

713
01:08:54,350 --> 01:08:56,889
You have been proven guilty, Oktem Bey.

714
01:09:03,250 --> 01:09:04,990
I don't know about this.

715
01:09:12,000 --> 01:09:13,770
It must be them...
They slandered us.

716
01:09:16,479 --> 01:09:18,700
They set their game
a long time ago, Turgut Bey.

717
01:09:27,720 --> 01:09:31,380
What happens next will be decided
by the court.

718
01:09:33,979 --> 01:09:34,990
Good.

719
01:09:48,600 --> 01:09:50,229
Have you hidden the gold well?

720
01:09:50,680 --> 01:09:53,080
I hid it when I was
on my night shift, madam.

721
01:09:55,020 --> 01:09:57,380
I would take a bit of you with me...

722
01:09:58,660 --> 01:10:01,160
...if Leo wasn't going to give me much more.

723
01:10:03,900 --> 01:10:05,310
Attaboy.

724
01:10:06,270 --> 01:10:08,650
So you have been working with Leo
for long years.

725
01:10:13,070 --> 01:10:15,160
So you did bring the dungeon's map, huh?

726
01:10:15,160 --> 01:10:16,430
Yes ma'am

727
01:10:16,510 --> 01:10:17,560
Where is Mr. Leo?

728
01:10:17,860 --> 01:10:19,370
I haven't seen him.

729
01:10:20,320 --> 01:10:23,720
I'll give you your reward in return of
your service for Leo.

730
01:10:54,440 --> 01:10:56,300
Do you hear the sound of death?

731
01:10:59,970 --> 01:11:01,100
You do not.

732
01:11:05,700 --> 01:11:08,450
Yenisehir.

733
01:11:09,060 --> 01:11:11,250
Did I hear right, mother?

734
01:11:12,830 --> 01:11:14,500
Did they kidnap my brother?

735
01:11:14,540 --> 01:11:18,370
Your father went after them,
Aladdin will return safely, Inshallah.

736
01:11:18,400 --> 01:11:20,580
Mother, Alps are waiting outside.

737
01:11:21,060 --> 01:11:23,190
Order me to bring my brother back!

738
01:11:23,570 --> 01:11:26,640
We don't need that, my brave son.

739
01:11:27,500 --> 01:11:29,700
You will meet your brother soon.

740
01:11:30,370 --> 01:11:32,450
Are you saying this to stop me, mother?

741
01:11:32,670 --> 01:11:34,750
Why would I want to stop Bey Orhan?

742
01:11:35,010 --> 01:11:37,920
So what about all the alps
who fill the tribe?

743
01:12:23,120 --> 01:12:25,360
Malhun Hatun, Kantakuzenos has arrived.

744
01:12:34,260 --> 01:12:34,980
Let him.

745
01:13:06,420 --> 01:13:07,680
Malhun Hatun.

746
01:13:09,950 --> 01:13:11,020
Orhan Bey.

747
01:13:11,920 --> 01:13:13,970
I salute you both with respect.

748
01:13:15,650 --> 01:13:17,170
Welcome.

749
01:13:17,310 --> 01:13:19,200
Osman Bey will be here shortly.

750
01:13:19,390 --> 01:13:21,520
You can wait in the entrance tent.

751
01:13:22,540 --> 01:13:24,500
He won't make it anyway.

752
01:13:24,750 --> 01:13:26,750
Of course.

753
01:13:27,890 --> 01:13:30,610
What is the reason for your visit,
Kantakuzenos?

754
01:13:32,640 --> 01:13:35,060
I hosted Osman Bey in my city.

755
01:13:36,560 --> 01:13:38,770
I wanted to return the visit.

756
01:13:39,980 --> 01:13:42,800
And of course,
there is that court issue.

757
01:13:43,490 --> 01:13:47,600
I hope you have nothing to do with the
abduction of my brother.

758
01:13:50,210 --> 01:13:51,920
Don't worry little Bey.

759
01:13:52,610 --> 01:13:56,750
I hope your father will come back
with your brother safely.

760
01:13:57,260 --> 01:13:59,820
Osman Bey is coming.

761
01:14:08,220 --> 01:14:09,310
Brother.

762
01:14:19,020 --> 01:14:22,030
Son, son!

763
01:14:30,260 --> 01:14:31,260
Brother.

764
01:14:35,310 --> 01:14:38,270
- Welcome, Osman Bey.
- Welcome to you.

765
01:14:38,930 --> 01:14:40,270
You are the guest.

766
01:14:42,700 --> 01:14:45,700
I am so glad you found your son
and came back safe and sound

767
01:14:49,710 --> 01:14:52,900
All this happened after
you and Olof came.

768
01:14:54,220 --> 01:14:56,540
They tried to kill our children.

769
01:15:01,150 --> 01:15:02,830
They set a trap on us.

770
01:15:03,470 --> 01:15:05,820
This didn't start because I or Olof came.

771
01:15:06,960 --> 01:15:10,210
It all started after you saved the emperor.

772
01:15:10,290 --> 01:15:12,210
Alright then, I'll finish it.

773
01:15:13,340 --> 01:15:15,440
That's exactly why I'm here.

774
01:15:16,240 --> 01:15:19,420
I want Frigg and Ophelia to
get the ending they deserve.

775
01:15:22,210 --> 01:15:23,950
Ophelia is there

776
01:15:25,390 --> 01:15:26,800
And the throne is there.

777
01:15:28,060 --> 01:15:29,570
Why are you here?

778
01:15:31,180 --> 01:15:33,280
Shouldn't you be next to the emperor?

779
01:15:33,470 --> 01:15:35,280
I am a servant of Rome.

780
01:15:35,980 --> 01:15:39,090
Oktem Bey's trial is justice for Rome.

781
01:15:39,680 --> 01:15:41,690
This is as important as the throne.

782
01:15:41,710 --> 01:15:46,350
We do not need the justice of Rome
while we have our justice.

783
01:15:47,230 --> 01:15:49,060
What's gonna happen,
is gonna happen.

784
01:15:51,860 --> 01:15:54,620
My Bey, its from Turgut Bey.

785
01:16:21,470 --> 01:16:24,260
Gold was found in Oktem Bey's tribe.

786
01:16:28,050 --> 01:16:30,480
What you said happened, Kantakuzenos.

787
01:16:30,940 --> 01:16:34,260
So you'll hand me Oktam Bey,
won't you?

788
01:16:34,720 --> 01:16:36,870
He committed the crime against you.

789
01:16:38,860 --> 01:16:41,220
But he is from us.

790
01:16:43,220 --> 01:16:45,120
Let's meet in the tribe
of Oktem Bey tomorrow.

791
01:16:46,050 --> 01:16:48,400
I will punish him myself.

792
01:16:48,640 --> 01:16:52,180
I don't care about the rest if
you punish him in front of me

793
01:16:52,980 --> 01:16:55,680
- Then see you tomorrow.
- Go well.

794
01:17:10,160 --> 01:17:12,260
- Boran
- My Bey!

795
01:17:14,080 --> 01:17:16,640
Invite everyone to the court.

796
01:17:37,920 --> 01:17:40,000
As you order, my Bey.

797
01:17:40,260 --> 01:17:42,720
I will take revenge on Osman, Olof.

798
01:17:42,980 --> 01:17:44,720
Don't worry brother.

799
01:17:45,620 --> 01:17:48,640
Our friend already avenged us.

800
01:17:49,180 --> 01:17:51,180
Osman and his son died.

801
01:17:54,050 --> 01:17:55,620
Vengeance!

802
01:17:56,820 --> 01:17:59,280
It will not end with Osman's death!

803
01:18:00,300 --> 01:18:06,510
Every Turk I will kill from now on
will go into the grave without a finger!

804
01:18:07,780 --> 01:18:09,020
Do you...

805
01:18:11,180 --> 01:18:14,140
Do you think that they will have graves?

806
01:18:14,590 --> 01:18:19,470
They will be food for crows!

807
01:18:29,810 --> 01:18:31,250
We lost

808
01:18:37,300 --> 01:18:39,170
What did we lose?

809
01:18:41,360 --> 01:18:42,500
The trap...

810
01:18:43,390 --> 01:18:45,140
They set a trap for us, Olof!

811
01:18:47,460 --> 01:18:49,870
Is Osman alive?

812
01:18:51,090 --> 01:18:53,630
You were going to avenge Saga!

813
01:18:54,540 --> 01:18:57,300
You were going to avenge our men!

814
01:18:57,580 --> 01:19:01,730
And I lost my brother Lef, Olof!

815
01:19:03,420 --> 01:19:05,740
Now our vengance is greater!

816
01:19:08,220 --> 01:19:11,860
I will avenge with my own hands, Olof!

817
01:19:14,460 --> 01:19:16,240
Give me one more chance.

818
01:19:17,040 --> 01:19:21,730
We will take revenge with
Kantakuzenos' army.

819
01:19:21,730 --> 01:19:23,090
How will this happen?

820
01:19:33,140 --> 01:19:37,040
Kantakuzenos poisoned the emperor.

821
01:19:39,740 --> 01:19:42,030
Ophelia will be held responsible.

822
01:19:42,720 --> 01:19:45,730
And since Ophelia will die as a traitor...

823
01:19:46,110 --> 01:19:48,500
...the throne will be Kantakuzenos'.

824
01:19:53,810 --> 01:19:56,270
And the army of vengeance will be ours.

825
01:20:14,210 --> 01:20:15,620
You are safe here.

826
01:20:16,130 --> 01:20:18,050
Have you seen my father, Sarkis?

827
01:20:24,750 --> 01:20:27,010
What do the soldiers want from you,
princess?

828
01:20:27,310 --> 01:20:28,960
Why are you running away?

829
01:20:30,500 --> 01:20:34,910
They did something to my father, Sarkis.

830
01:20:36,180 --> 01:20:37,980
Maybe they killed him.

831
01:20:39,070 --> 01:20:43,280
Whoever did this is trying to
put the blame on me!

832
01:20:45,630 --> 01:20:49,700
Whoever attacked the arena did this as well.

833
01:20:52,560 --> 01:20:54,400
Someone who wants the throne.

834
01:20:56,800 --> 01:21:00,060
You shouldn't stay in the palace,
it's not safe here.

835
01:21:00,960 --> 01:21:03,950
How? What should I do?

836
01:21:04,510 --> 01:21:08,080
My father?
What about my father?

837
01:21:14,240 --> 01:21:16,980
I have to get to my father!
They must have poisoned him!

838
01:21:16,980 --> 01:21:18,400
Oh princess.

839
01:21:18,560 --> 01:21:21,630
If they poisoned your father,
you won't be able to help him

840
01:21:23,200 --> 01:21:24,400
What should I do?

841
01:21:25,260 --> 01:21:27,520
You should hide somewhere
they can't find you.

842
01:21:28,100 --> 01:21:29,520
And I will ask for help.

843
01:21:30,260 --> 01:21:31,520
From whom?

844
01:21:34,540 --> 01:21:36,540
From someone who helped us before.

845
01:21:42,050 --> 01:21:46,100
What we are experiencing now
is because of the tasks of Osman Bey.

846
01:21:50,750 --> 01:21:55,700
Osman Bey wants the interest of Beys
and all this is for the sake of conquests.

847
01:21:55,800 --> 01:21:58,700
Who could have known that
such a calamity would happen?

848
01:21:58,770 --> 01:22:01,020
Osman Bey will rule with justice.

849
01:22:02,240 --> 01:22:03,700
Trust him.

850
01:22:05,390 --> 01:22:07,390
Please be comfortable.

851
01:22:08,690 --> 01:22:10,240
I do not trust anybody.

852
01:22:10,400 --> 01:22:13,100
I don't make the same mistake
my father has done, Subasi.

853
01:22:20,850 --> 01:22:22,590
Your anger is not good, Alcicek.

854
01:22:25,860 --> 01:22:27,450
You know what it causes.

855
01:22:29,750 --> 01:22:31,270
It happened unintentionally.

856
01:22:32,210 --> 01:22:33,770
You have to get out quickly

857
01:22:34,900 --> 01:22:35,940
Come on

858
01:22:36,100 --> 01:22:37,730
Before the alps come!

859
01:22:37,730 --> 01:22:39,670
You can't think about me right now!

860
01:22:47,550 --> 01:22:49,530
You should see a healer!

861
01:22:50,260 --> 01:22:51,730
It's not important.

862
01:22:52,230 --> 01:22:54,220
Come on, get out.

863
01:23:01,690 --> 01:23:03,120
I keep the dagger.

864
01:23:04,470 --> 01:23:06,460
What you are doing is unpredictable.

865
01:23:07,310 --> 01:23:10,710
You might get angry now
and stab him in my heart

866
01:23:14,880 --> 01:23:16,020
You have a wound, man!

867
01:23:16,530 --> 01:23:17,650
Why are you laughing for?

868
01:23:20,320 --> 01:23:21,930
Come on, Alcicek, get out!

869
01:23:22,170 --> 01:23:23,300
Come on.

870
01:23:37,830 --> 01:23:40,130
We have a lot to do with you,
Alcicek Hatun.

871
01:23:41,380 --> 01:23:44,210
Are you still talking about
such a small wound?!

872
01:23:46,000 --> 01:23:47,920
How coward you are, Subasi!

873
01:23:57,100 --> 01:23:58,200
Leave me.

874
01:24:01,030 --> 01:24:02,810
I told you to leave me, Subasi!

875
01:24:05,660 --> 01:24:06,970
Subasi, leave my hand

876
01:24:25,630 --> 01:24:26,690
You are right.

877
01:24:29,500 --> 01:24:30,610
I'm a coward.

878
01:24:33,040 --> 01:24:35,260
I am the one who scares seven countries.

879
01:24:36,290 --> 01:24:37,690
Aktemur, son of Gunduz Bey.

880
01:24:39,890 --> 01:24:42,000
Subasi Aktemur.

881
01:24:46,490 --> 01:24:48,960
My limbs tremble when
I look into your eyes

882
01:24:51,580 --> 01:24:52,870
I am so afraid, Alcicek.

883
01:25:03,630 --> 01:25:05,030
But you are also afraid!

884
01:25:10,190 --> 01:25:11,950
You can't even say my name!

885
01:25:33,160 --> 01:25:35,400
They kidnapped my son in my town!

886
01:25:38,610 --> 01:25:39,890
And they didn't stop there.

887
01:25:41,230 --> 01:25:42,920
They also took him prisoner.

888
01:25:45,870 --> 01:25:47,030
Tell me now.

889
01:25:47,980 --> 01:25:49,910
Which one of you will pay for this?

890
01:26:01,160 --> 01:26:02,880
Are you going to pay?

891
01:26:04,870 --> 01:26:05,960
Huh?

892
01:26:09,500 --> 01:26:11,160
- Or will you pay?
- My Bey...

893
01:26:11,240 --> 01:26:13,620
- We were changing the tor...
- Shut up!

894
01:26:17,510 --> 01:26:19,280
I don't want another excuse.

895
01:26:23,000 --> 01:26:25,060
In this path we have been dreaming of...

896
01:26:26,100 --> 01:26:27,920
...there shall be no mistake.

897
01:26:30,830 --> 01:26:32,560
You will continue

898
01:26:33,790 --> 01:26:35,610
You will keep searching.

899
01:26:35,960 --> 01:26:37,740
As you order, my Bey!

900
01:26:40,350 --> 01:26:41,520
Get out now.

901
01:27:03,140 --> 01:27:04,570
There is a message from Konur.

902
01:27:06,280 --> 01:27:07,840
I will go to Constantinople.

903
01:27:08,610 --> 01:27:11,510
They want to poison the emperor
and accuse Ophelia.

904
01:27:12,410 --> 01:27:14,120
Can we trust Ophelia, my Bey?

905
01:27:14,490 --> 01:27:17,520
We'll know who we can trust
after we take Ophelia.

906
01:27:17,810 --> 01:27:19,180
My Bey, I have prepared the alps.

907
01:27:19,280 --> 01:27:21,270
I will only go with Kumral Abdal.

908
01:27:25,000 --> 01:27:26,590
While I am taking Ophelia...

909
01:27:27,340 --> 01:27:28,940
..he will cure the emperor

910
01:27:29,740 --> 01:27:31,070
You can go out.

911
01:27:31,070 --> 01:27:32,280
Yes my Bey.

912
01:27:38,930 --> 01:27:40,040
My Bey.

913
01:27:42,190 --> 01:27:43,340
Subasi Aktemur.

914
01:27:44,040 --> 01:27:46,150
He was on a mission in Oktem Bey's tribe.

915
01:27:47,330 --> 01:27:49,650
I am the only reason
why the prisoner escaped.

916
01:27:52,300 --> 01:27:54,080
That escaper...

917
01:27:55,010 --> 01:27:56,770
..he tried to kill our son.

918
01:27:58,870 --> 01:28:00,360
He is free for now.

919
01:28:01,440 --> 01:28:02,780
But do not worry.

920
01:28:03,300 --> 01:28:04,520
His life won't last long.

921
01:28:06,170 --> 01:28:07,690
Take extra precautions.

922
01:28:31,330 --> 01:28:32,560
My brave son.

923
01:28:33,990 --> 01:28:35,770
You did not surrender to the enemy.

924
01:28:36,160 --> 01:28:38,440
You resisted to honor your father.

925
01:28:39,470 --> 01:28:40,640
Praise be!

926
01:28:42,460 --> 01:28:43,950
Sorry, mother.

927
01:28:45,710 --> 01:28:46,970
I've caused you trouble.

928
01:28:48,540 --> 01:28:50,090
I should have been careful.

929
01:28:52,660 --> 01:28:54,040
Don't say that, son.

930
01:28:57,660 --> 01:29:01,250
You cannot do anything
when the enemy attacks from behind...

931
01:29:02,100 --> 01:29:03,280
Can I?

932
01:29:05,420 --> 01:29:07,010
Come in Orhan, come in.

933
01:29:24,160 --> 01:29:26,100
I will check your sister.

934
01:29:53,450 --> 01:29:55,180
- Brother
- Brother

935
01:30:06,440 --> 01:30:07,750
You look healthy, brother.

936
01:30:08,240 --> 01:30:09,390
I'm fine brother.

937
01:30:10,420 --> 01:30:12,640
They attacked me before,
now they attack you.

938
01:30:16,250 --> 01:30:19,160
We are at death's door,
we shall end the conflict.

939
01:30:19,500 --> 01:30:21,510
There is no conflict between us, brother.

940
01:30:23,270 --> 01:30:24,440
It's just...

941
01:30:25,000 --> 01:30:26,480
Just what brother?

942
01:30:29,420 --> 01:30:32,010
There cannot be any conflict
between brothers!

943
01:30:36,100 --> 01:30:37,660
How is your hand?

944
01:30:38,100 --> 01:30:40,110
It is getting better.

945
01:30:43,690 --> 01:30:45,120
Take this dagger.

946
01:30:50,170 --> 01:30:51,970
You deserve it, brother.

947
01:30:53,290 --> 01:30:55,550
They attack you to kill you.

948
01:30:55,970 --> 01:30:57,840
They attack me to capture me.

949
01:31:00,950 --> 01:31:03,250
Even the enemy is not intrested in me.

950
01:31:08,940 --> 01:31:10,660
So always keep this with yourself.

951
01:31:11,530 --> 01:31:13,410
So that this won't happen again.

952
01:31:20,680 --> 01:31:23,300
Come on, have a rest.

953
01:31:54,900 --> 01:31:55,910
Malhun?

954
01:31:56,920 --> 01:31:58,160
Can I come in?

955
01:31:59,520 --> 01:32:01,630
Come, Bala, come.

956
01:32:13,060 --> 01:32:14,200
Bengi Hatun.

957
01:32:15,810 --> 01:32:18,100
She buried Batur today.

958
01:32:19,640 --> 01:32:22,290
Every time I think about it,
my heart burns, Bala.

959
01:32:24,860 --> 01:32:27,210
Allah shall never let anyone
go through that.

960
01:32:30,550 --> 01:32:32,430
Children feel different, Malhun.

961
01:32:33,110 --> 01:32:34,680
When their nail hurts...

962
01:32:35,270 --> 01:32:36,900
...your heart shatters.

963
01:32:46,010 --> 01:32:47,520
Time flies.

964
01:32:48,250 --> 01:32:49,900
How small he was!

965
01:32:51,120 --> 01:32:52,860
And now he's become a great Bey!

966
01:32:54,230 --> 01:32:56,040
I sewed it for Orhan, right?

967
01:33:00,830 --> 01:33:02,670
What if I had lost Orhan, Bala?

968
01:33:04,350 --> 01:33:08,140
Whenever I remember, I feel like my mind
and heart are going out of their place!

969
01:33:08,140 --> 01:33:10,010
What if I couldn't catch up?

970
01:33:12,040 --> 01:33:14,990
What if I was the one who buried her son?

971
01:33:21,190 --> 01:33:23,670
When I saw Aladdin's bloody hat...

972
01:33:25,310 --> 01:33:29,110
I thought I wouldn't be able to live
with that pain, I would die.

973
01:33:31,590 --> 01:33:33,090
I wanted to scream.

974
01:33:33,400 --> 01:33:35,420
I wanted to make the world shake.

975
01:33:36,130 --> 01:33:37,660
I couldn't scream.

976
01:33:38,310 --> 01:33:39,890
I couldn't scream

977
01:33:40,640 --> 01:33:42,590
All those Alps behind me...

978
01:33:43,230 --> 01:33:45,480
I hid the pain of my heart
behind my weapon.

979
01:33:46,130 --> 01:33:47,980
Then I tried to save my son.

980
01:33:54,830 --> 01:33:58,300
The destiny of our children was already
written before they were born.

981
01:34:00,130 --> 01:34:02,350
We have saved them from countless enemies.

982
01:34:04,220 --> 01:34:05,940
And many more are to come.

983
01:34:09,180 --> 01:34:10,660
Malhun Hatun...

984
01:34:12,380 --> 01:34:14,770
Your children are my children.

985
01:34:15,550 --> 01:34:17,150
Never forget this.

986
01:34:22,460 --> 01:34:24,650
Not to speak of being jealous...

987
01:34:25,070 --> 01:34:27,810
I am ready to burn the whole world
for our children.

988
01:34:28,020 --> 01:34:30,320
We are not just wives of Osman Bey.

989
01:34:31,220 --> 01:34:33,330
We are not just his warriors.

990
01:34:35,090 --> 01:34:37,730
We are the mothers of
the almighty state!

991
01:34:44,910 --> 01:34:46,500
Even if our hearts burn...

992
01:34:47,630 --> 01:34:50,990
Our almighty state and our case
comes first.

993
01:34:52,160 --> 01:34:53,810
And then our children...

994
01:34:53,810 --> 01:34:55,810
Then our motherhood.

995
01:34:56,320 --> 01:34:57,490
That's right.

996
01:34:58,740 --> 01:35:02,530
We would sacrifice a thousand children
for this state.

997
01:35:04,750 --> 01:35:06,530
Even if our hearts burn...

998
01:35:07,470 --> 01:35:11,870
Our job as mothers of the state
comes before all else.

999
01:35:13,460 --> 01:35:17,380
Thank Allah, our valiants stand together.

1000
01:35:17,780 --> 01:35:19,380
They stand tall like mountains.

1001
01:35:19,660 --> 01:35:22,130
We will stand together too.

1002
01:35:22,130 --> 01:35:24,130
Surely.

1003
01:35:25,810 --> 01:35:30,420
We will do this in order for
this almighty state to live forever

1004
01:35:32,110 --> 01:35:33,870
This is our duty.

1005
01:35:35,540 --> 01:35:37,200
This is our destiny.

1006
01:35:42,340 --> 01:35:43,710
Enough already!

1007
01:35:43,710 --> 01:35:45,710
At any cost...

1008
01:35:45,710 --> 01:35:47,710
...this time I will tell him

1009
01:35:54,580 --> 01:35:57,470
I would look after his children.

1010
01:36:03,420 --> 01:36:05,330
What if he condemns me?

1011
01:36:07,540 --> 01:36:10,320
Is there anything wrong with love?

1012
01:36:10,560 --> 01:36:11,490
No!

1013
01:36:12,850 --> 01:36:15,040
No, I will tell him.

1014
01:36:15,900 --> 01:36:18,430
Hey you! Cerkutay!

1015
01:36:19,200 --> 01:36:20,690
Love ya!

1016
01:36:22,050 --> 01:36:23,120
I will say it.

1017
01:36:38,110 --> 01:36:39,810
Smells nice.

1018
01:36:40,660 --> 01:36:42,690
This will ease my job.

1019
01:37:03,730 --> 01:37:05,100
Hungry I am!

1020
01:37:11,010 --> 01:37:12,640
I can't hear!

1021
01:37:18,460 --> 01:37:19,470
I can't hear.

1022
01:38:23,280 --> 01:38:24,940
Cerkutay!

1023
01:38:34,290 --> 01:38:35,940
Eat, Cerkutay, eat

1024
01:38:41,700 --> 01:38:42,590
Eat.

1025
01:38:44,020 --> 01:38:47,620
Eat but.. Listen to me too,
okay?

1026
01:38:50,060 --> 01:38:53,070
I know that a Hatun
usually doesn't say that.

1027
01:38:53,070 --> 01:38:54,140
But..

1028
01:38:54,500 --> 01:38:55,580
I'll say it!

1029
01:39:12,030 --> 01:39:13,300
Bon Apetit!

1030
01:39:13,300 --> 01:39:14,800
Let me fill it back!

1031
01:39:14,800 --> 01:39:17,180
I will bring more!

1032
01:39:24,340 --> 01:39:27,060
The comfort lies in silence.

1033
01:39:33,500 --> 01:39:34,540
Enjoy it.

1034
01:39:40,000 --> 01:39:42,030
What I mean is...

1035
01:39:42,350 --> 01:39:43,680
Cerkutay...

1036
01:39:44,990 --> 01:39:47,630
I.. I will tell you...

1037
01:39:49,170 --> 01:39:50,930
I am in love with you!

1038
01:40:00,080 --> 01:40:01,250
Cerkutay!

1039
01:40:04,670 --> 01:40:05,920
Let's get out!

1040
01:40:17,840 --> 01:40:19,360
Cerkutay!!!!

1041
01:40:19,940 --> 01:40:21,940
I'm telling you, we're going brother!

1042
01:40:22,130 --> 01:40:24,530
What are you saying
I don't hear I don't hear!

1043
01:40:25,330 --> 01:40:27,300
We'll go brother, come on!

1044
01:40:27,310 --> 01:40:29,370
Go on, brother. Godspeed!
Go well.

1045
01:40:33,420 --> 01:40:36,080
Come on brother, come on,
you're coming with me.

1046
01:40:37,890 --> 01:40:38,830
Come on.

1047
01:40:43,090 --> 01:40:43,920
Come on.

1048
01:40:45,330 --> 01:40:46,270
Come on brother.

1049
01:40:46,270 --> 01:40:47,180
Boran!

1050
01:40:47,180 --> 01:40:49,180
Yes brother, yes.

1051
01:40:49,390 --> 01:40:52,830
Keep this.
Don't eat it. I'll eat it later.

1052
01:40:52,830 --> 01:40:53,950
Okay brother.

1053
01:40:53,950 --> 01:40:55,020
Boran Alp!

1054
01:40:55,950 --> 01:41:00,260
Is Cerkutay deaf?

1055
01:41:02,930 --> 01:41:04,610
Unfortunately, Ulgen sister.

1056
01:41:05,010 --> 01:41:06,610
His ears are no longer working.

1057
01:41:07,600 --> 01:41:09,440
But don't be sad, it's temporary.

1058
01:41:09,680 --> 01:41:11,790
Come on.

1059
01:41:11,810 --> 01:41:14,100
- So delicious!
- Come on, come on.

1060
01:41:18,130 --> 01:41:21,830
Have I been talking in vain?!?

1061
01:41:23,150 --> 01:41:25,390
How unlucky I am!

1062
01:41:49,950 --> 01:41:51,340
Aladdin.

1063
01:42:05,230 --> 01:42:06,980
My valiant son.

1064
01:42:11,070 --> 01:42:13,060
My miracle kid.

1065
01:42:22,060 --> 01:42:23,140
Aladdin.

1066
01:42:24,740 --> 01:42:27,940
I do not differentiate between my children.

1067
01:42:31,250 --> 01:42:33,520
A father's heart is so big...

1068
01:42:36,260 --> 01:42:38,180
...that there is a place for all of you.

1069
01:42:40,850 --> 01:42:43,540
You are like tree branches.

1070
01:42:44,370 --> 01:42:48,530
Together but in different.

1071
01:42:51,090 --> 01:42:52,640
Your characters...

1072
01:42:54,020 --> 01:42:56,660
... and your skills
are different from each other

1073
01:43:01,810 --> 01:43:03,100
Son.

1074
01:43:05,540 --> 01:43:07,900
Never forget this.

1075
01:43:21,600 --> 01:43:23,550
I've heard it all, father.

1076
01:43:24,530 --> 01:43:28,560
Why would I tell you if I thought
you wouldn't hear it, son?

1077
01:43:29,890 --> 01:43:31,280
I knew you weren't asleep.

1078
01:43:43,070 --> 01:43:44,450
Where are you going?

1079
01:43:47,310 --> 01:43:48,990
To the infidels.

1080
01:43:49,580 --> 01:43:52,060
To give you a safe homeland.

1081
01:43:52,720 --> 01:43:54,060
However...

1082
01:43:54,060 --> 01:43:56,060
...keeping this state safe...

1083
01:43:56,960 --> 01:43:58,830
...is your duty.

1084
01:43:59,300 --> 01:44:03,110
You shouldn't feel despair
and give up.

1085
01:44:03,200 --> 01:44:05,200
You will get up on your feet.

1086
01:44:06,800 --> 01:44:08,480
And you will be patient.

1087
01:44:11,700 --> 01:44:13,680
Patience brings salvation.

1088
01:44:15,900 --> 01:44:17,420
Patience brings...

1089
01:44:19,220 --> 01:44:21,230
...an eternal state.

1090
01:44:24,160 --> 01:44:25,620
And that country...

1091
01:44:26,290 --> 01:44:27,970
...in your hands...

1092
01:44:29,540 --> 01:44:31,490
...will rule the whole world.

1093
01:44:54,460 --> 01:44:56,480
Trust me, father.

1094
01:45:00,540 --> 01:45:01,920
The horses are ready, my Bey.

1095
01:45:02,530 --> 01:45:03,920
Eyvallah (Thanks).

1096
01:45:07,300 --> 01:45:09,000
Where are you going, Cerkutay?

1097
01:45:09,940 --> 01:45:11,200
YES MY BEY!

1098
01:45:12,070 --> 01:45:13,520
What is he saying?

1099
01:45:14,440 --> 01:45:16,520
My Bey, he still can't hear.

1100
01:45:19,850 --> 01:45:20,850
Obviously.

1101
01:45:21,790 --> 01:45:23,500
He still can't hear.

1102
01:45:25,300 --> 01:45:26,810
Go to Oktem Bey...

1103
01:45:29,930 --> 01:45:31,970
Go to Oktem Bey's tribe tomorrow.

1104
01:45:32,740 --> 01:45:34,560
Side with Turgut Bey.

1105
01:45:34,920 --> 01:45:36,180
As you order my Bey.

1106
01:45:36,350 --> 01:45:37,530
Agreed, my Bey!

1107
01:45:43,370 --> 01:45:44,790
Brother!

1108
01:45:47,460 --> 01:45:49,350
Brother!

1109
01:45:49,920 --> 01:45:51,350
Cerkutay.

1110
01:45:52,070 --> 01:45:55,020
We are not going.

1111
01:45:55,820 --> 01:45:57,630
Stop, Cerkutay.

1112
01:46:03,180 --> 01:46:05,810
Oktam's Tribe

1113
01:46:11,980 --> 01:46:14,860
My Allah shall forbid
anyone going through this.

1114
01:46:17,030 --> 01:46:19,350
Slander hits hard.

1115
01:46:20,160 --> 01:46:22,980
They casted us down.

1116
01:46:24,610 --> 01:46:26,920
They took our liver.

1117
01:46:27,500 --> 01:46:29,190
This despair...

1118
01:46:31,660 --> 01:46:35,480
...doesn't fit in us, Oktem Bey.

1119
01:46:37,900 --> 01:46:39,450
No it's not.

1120
01:46:44,130 --> 01:46:45,560
Thank you.

1121
01:46:55,120 --> 01:47:00,140
The reason for everything that happened is
Osman Bey.

1122
01:47:01,300 --> 01:47:06,110
We are paying the price
for him to found a state.

1123
01:47:07,660 --> 01:47:13,150
But this is not going to end well.

1124
01:47:16,170 --> 01:47:17,910
I do not trust Osman at all.

1125
01:47:20,750 --> 01:47:22,880
He will unite with the infidels.

1126
01:47:24,440 --> 01:47:26,540
They will burn your father, Alcicek.

1127
01:47:30,140 --> 01:47:32,340
Just like how they burned Batur...

1128
01:47:33,950 --> 01:47:35,800
...they will burn your father too.

1129
01:47:37,170 --> 01:47:38,200
Mother...

1130
01:47:39,850 --> 01:47:41,700
...what if what we're doing is wrong?

1131
01:47:43,080 --> 01:47:46,030
...what if it is best to trust Osman Bey?

1132
01:47:47,350 --> 01:47:48,420
You know...

1133
01:47:49,320 --> 01:47:52,280
My father thought well of him all the time.

1134
01:47:52,780 --> 01:47:54,470
He helped us a lot

1135
01:47:55,220 --> 01:47:57,990
Now why would he hurt my father?

1136
01:47:57,990 --> 01:48:02,440
The same reason why he hurt Batur, Alcicek!

1137
01:48:05,230 --> 01:48:08,990
And now will he
stand against the emperor...

1138
01:48:09,610 --> 01:48:11,890
...and stand with your father, huh?

1139
01:48:13,560 --> 01:48:15,680
Is it only me...

1140
01:48:16,620 --> 01:48:18,780
....who has gone through all these?

1141
01:48:20,710 --> 01:48:23,470
What trust are you talking about, Alcicek?

1142
01:48:25,910 --> 01:48:27,550
Let me clear the table.

1143
01:48:35,480 --> 01:48:39,630
I know what to do.

1144
01:48:46,910 --> 01:48:48,630
Sent by Osman Bey, my Bey.

1145
01:48:59,890 --> 01:49:01,540
Osman Bey is not coming.

1146
01:49:02,950 --> 01:49:05,270
He says don't let Kantakuzenos
take Oktem Bey.

1147
01:49:07,520 --> 01:49:09,510
I hope there's nothing wrong.

1148
01:49:09,790 --> 01:49:12,470
Constantinople

1149
01:49:20,490 --> 01:49:22,810
We will attack the enemy from here.

1150
01:49:25,800 --> 01:49:27,480
Are you afraid, Kumral Abdal?

1151
01:49:29,030 --> 01:49:33,000
You don't take the
cowards with you, Osman Bey!

1152
01:49:33,110 --> 01:49:34,400
That's right.

1153
01:49:35,070 --> 01:49:37,350
Also, with Sari Saltug, we have...

1154
01:49:38,180 --> 01:49:41,040
...experienced a lot
in the lands of infidels!

1155
01:49:41,040 --> 01:49:42,390
But Osman Bey...

1156
01:49:42,550 --> 01:49:45,930
We toured all their lands
and never saw anything like this.

1157
01:49:46,600 --> 01:49:47,750
Nice.

1158
01:49:48,060 --> 01:49:49,750
The city is nice too.

1159
01:49:50,190 --> 01:49:51,590
But its rulers aren't.

1160
01:49:52,020 --> 01:49:54,260
We will give them a lesson.

1161
01:49:56,430 --> 01:49:58,310
- Is it only two of us?
- Let's go.

1162
01:50:07,770 --> 01:50:08,800
Come on.

1163
01:50:14,560 --> 01:50:16,540
The end of the world is coming, my Sheik.

1164
01:50:17,230 --> 01:50:24,370
Humanity is deceived by Satan all the time.

1165
01:50:24,860 --> 01:50:30,950
A brother envies another.

1166
01:50:32,670 --> 01:50:38,170
You are talking about the envy that
throw Yusuf in the well, right?

1167
01:50:38,420 --> 01:50:40,930
The envy that befell that beautiful prophet...

1168
01:50:43,800 --> 01:50:45,680
...will do anything to us, my Sheik.

1169
01:50:49,650 --> 01:50:54,210
Yusuf's brothers were deceived by satan.

1170
01:50:55,660 --> 01:50:57,040
They were so deceived.

1171
01:50:57,940 --> 01:51:04,740
Our master Yakup's love for Yusuf,
peace be upon him, was so great.

1172
01:51:05,880 --> 01:51:11,300
His brothers were angry and jealous of him.

1173
01:51:11,610 --> 01:51:16,630
They were jealous so much that
they thought of killing their brother.

1174
01:51:19,020 --> 01:51:21,220
They tried to kill him.

1175
01:51:22,670 --> 01:51:28,480
They took the beautiful-faced Prophet
with them and threw him into a well.

1176
01:51:29,160 --> 01:51:36,420
Then they stained his shirt with blood
and give it to his father, our master Yakup

1177
01:51:36,780 --> 01:51:40,190
They said that "Yusuf was eaten by a wolf...

1178
01:51:41,380 --> 01:51:45,300
...Yusuf is no longer with us, he died."

1179
01:51:46,090 --> 01:51:51,190
As soon as our master Yakup grabbed
Yusuf's shirt in his hand

1180
01:51:52,290 --> 01:51:53,640
He figured it out at that exact moment.

1181
01:51:55,040 --> 01:51:58,690
That Yusuf's brothers were lying.

1182
01:51:59,440 --> 01:52:08,580
And after that day, Prophet Yakup went blind
because of crying too much.

1183
01:52:09,530 --> 01:52:11,550
He said "the eyes that do not see Yusuf...

1184
01:52:12,350 --> 01:52:14,680
...shall not see the world either."

1185
01:52:15,640 --> 01:52:19,700
Joseph's brothers were jealous of their
father's love for Yusuf...

1186
01:52:19,700 --> 01:52:23,200
And they threw him in the well, right?

1187
01:52:23,610 --> 01:52:29,520
But they caused the greatest pain
of their father.

1188
01:52:30,690 --> 01:52:33,950
Their envy was so enormous that...

1189
01:52:34,810 --> 01:52:38,330
...they couldn't even tell the truth.

1190
01:52:39,450 --> 01:52:42,330
As for Yusuf, he came out of that well.

1191
01:52:43,270 --> 01:52:44,750
He became a slave.

1192
01:52:45,870 --> 01:52:49,700
He was slandered and imprisoned.

1193
01:52:49,840 --> 01:52:54,320
But he was always alive in Yakup's heart.

1194
01:52:54,840 --> 01:53:00,050
Yusuf got out of prison,
became Egypt's governor.

1195
01:53:02,020 --> 01:53:09,720
Someday, Yusuf's brothers went to him.

1196
01:53:10,190 --> 01:53:12,900
Yusuf recognized them.

1197
01:53:13,950 --> 01:53:15,870
And he confronted them.

1198
01:53:15,870 --> 01:53:20,660
But he did not despise them at all.

1199
01:53:22,660 --> 01:53:26,900
His brothers caused that beautiful face
prophet a heavy trouble...

1200
01:53:28,230 --> 01:53:34,790
...because of their envy against him.

1201
01:53:35,680 --> 01:53:41,220
As for him, he said to them
"You are not the one who brought me here"

1202
01:53:41,750 --> 01:53:43,420
"It is my Lord who brought me here"

1203
01:53:44,010 --> 01:53:47,630
His brothers asked for forgiveness from him.

1204
01:53:47,860 --> 01:53:54,310
They swore that Allah has placed you
in a higher rank than us.

1205
01:53:54,710 --> 01:54:00,100
We were certainly wrong, they said.

1206
01:54:01,530 --> 01:54:06,280
And they believed in the
prophethood of Yusuf, peace be upon him.

1207
01:54:06,460 --> 01:54:11,990
Hadrat Yusuf showed mercy to his brothers.

1208
01:54:12,130 --> 01:54:15,410
He went the way of The Most Merciful.

1209
01:54:15,750 --> 01:54:17,640
He forgave them.

1210
01:54:22,030 --> 01:54:27,920
He considered that everything
that happened to him was from Allah.

1211
01:54:28,460 --> 01:54:29,870
He didn't see any evil.

1212
01:54:30,060 --> 01:54:31,420
He was patient.

1213
01:54:31,620 --> 01:54:35,030
He was patient in the most beautiful way.

1214
01:54:38,390 --> 01:54:43,990
My dears, everything that Allah
has blessed us with is good.

1215
01:54:44,130 --> 01:54:48,580
We are sometimes sad about some incidents.

1216
01:54:48,820 --> 01:54:54,920
But in the end, the goodness inside
becomes clear to us.

1217
01:54:56,300 --> 01:55:02,550
The thing that keep prophet Yusuf alive
is his faith.

1218
01:55:04,430 --> 01:55:09,230
Life will pass through exams and hardships.

1219
01:55:09,480 --> 01:55:10,780
You should know this.

1220
01:55:11,670 --> 01:55:18,400
In every incident, you will go the way
the messengers of Allah went.

1221
01:55:18,660 --> 01:55:21,340
And you will find your light.

1222
01:55:22,230 --> 01:55:28,180
Prophet Yusuf is the one who forgave his
brothers who threw him into a well.

1223
01:55:29,060 --> 01:55:35,040
We shall not break anyone's heart.

1224
01:55:35,770 --> 01:55:37,440
Become a forgiver.

1225
01:55:38,020 --> 01:55:42,550
Let the verses of Allah and
the stories of his messengers...

1226
01:55:43,230 --> 01:55:52,800
And the honorable hadiths of our Messenger
guide you.

1227
01:55:53,260 --> 01:55:55,710
- Amen
- Amen

1228
01:55:57,810 --> 01:55:59,180
So, dears.

1229
01:56:00,270 --> 01:56:02,820
This was your class today.

1230
01:56:24,950 --> 01:56:27,070
My Bey, my Bey!
There is a sound!

1231
01:56:29,740 --> 01:56:30,630
My Bey!

1232
01:56:30,740 --> 01:56:31,860
No.

1233
01:56:47,850 --> 01:56:50,010
Did you think we were alone,
Kumral Abdal?

1234
01:56:50,330 --> 01:56:51,550
Check them!

1235
01:56:52,410 --> 01:56:54,560
In which city was the Turk left alone?!

1236
01:56:58,080 --> 01:57:02,000
The intelligence formations
that we established have begun to operate.

1237
01:57:07,340 --> 01:57:12,640
Praise be for the valiants and sisters!

1238
01:57:16,160 --> 01:57:19,710
My Bey, Olof's men are going to the arena,
they're getting ready.

1239
01:57:22,260 --> 01:57:25,010
I'm going to the arena.
You go to the palace.

1240
01:57:25,420 --> 01:57:27,250
Death and life comes from Allah.

1241
01:57:27,250 --> 01:57:31,860
But do your best to keep emperor alive so
no one we don't like sits on the throne.

1242
01:57:31,920 --> 01:57:34,960
I will do my best, if Allah permits, my Bey!

1243
01:57:35,500 --> 01:57:36,830
Let's go.

1244
01:57:57,710 --> 01:57:59,040
We are ready Olof.

1245
01:58:04,260 --> 01:58:05,890
We'll go to the arena.

1246
01:58:06,890 --> 01:58:10,940
Ophelia and dog Sarkis are there.

1247
01:58:12,690 --> 01:58:14,650
This will end today.

1248
01:58:16,120 --> 01:58:17,100
Come on.

1249
01:58:18,140 --> 01:58:20,820
Odin's ravens are going to kill!

1250
01:58:20,820 --> 01:58:23,230
We are coming!

1251
01:58:43,830 --> 01:58:45,040
I am a healer.

1252
01:58:45,730 --> 01:58:47,460
I came to heal him.

1253
01:58:48,100 --> 01:58:49,510
We can't get you inside.

1254
01:58:54,410 --> 01:58:59,030
I have to!
For the sake of the Emperor's health.

1255
01:59:03,150 --> 01:59:05,370
Check the door.
What is that noise about?

1256
01:59:10,060 --> 01:59:11,710
What's happening?
Who are you?

1257
01:59:14,330 --> 01:59:16,290
Soldiers, soldiers!

1258
01:59:21,600 --> 01:59:22,920
Sleep a while.

1259
01:59:26,800 --> 01:59:29,740
Emperor, Osman Bey sent me.

1260
01:59:31,020 --> 01:59:32,880
I came to heal you.

1261
01:59:33,240 --> 01:59:34,310
Osman Bey.

1262
01:59:34,310 --> 01:59:35,620
What is happening here?

1263
01:59:35,840 --> 01:59:37,220
Who are you?

1264
01:59:37,330 --> 01:59:38,320
Stop.

1265
01:59:41,560 --> 01:59:42,540
Let him.

1266
01:59:50,850 --> 01:59:57,080
Let's find out what kind of poison it is.

1267
02:00:10,880 --> 02:00:17,570
If there is life, there is hope.

1268
02:00:48,390 --> 02:00:51,060
What are those infidels doing here?

1269
02:00:54,220 --> 02:00:55,290
Leave!

1270
02:00:55,430 --> 02:00:57,980
Only thing we lacked was the infidels(!)

1271
02:00:57,990 --> 02:01:00,260
We'll solve this with peace, Oktem Bey.

1272
02:01:02,780 --> 02:01:05,740
They came again, what are they asking for?

1273
02:01:13,160 --> 02:01:14,190
Leave here!

1274
02:01:18,670 --> 02:01:19,700
Come on

1275
02:01:38,980 --> 02:01:40,190
Kantakuzenos.

1276
02:01:42,500 --> 02:01:43,390
Turgut Bey.

1277
02:01:46,390 --> 02:01:48,420
This incident will be solved today.

1278
02:01:50,110 --> 02:01:52,530
Gold came out of this tribe
as I heard

1279
02:01:53,870 --> 02:01:55,770
Given that the evidence is obvious...

1280
02:01:55,770 --> 02:01:57,130
Infidel!

1281
02:02:05,090 --> 02:02:06,620
You killed my alps!

1282
02:02:08,410 --> 02:02:10,380
You put gold in my tribe!

1283
02:02:12,130 --> 02:02:13,800
How dare you show up?

1284
02:02:18,400 --> 02:02:21,180
Come on, Kantakuzenos.
Let's go into the tent.

1285
02:02:22,610 --> 02:02:28,710
Will you invite this infidel to our tent
and host him too, Turgut Bey?

1286
02:02:29,860 --> 02:02:32,880
The blood of my uncle and our alps
is still on the ground!

1287
02:02:34,420 --> 02:02:39,790
I did not come to the tribe of someone
who killed my fellows...

1288
02:02:39,790 --> 02:02:42,300
...and stole my taxes.

1289
02:02:43,620 --> 02:02:44,850
Where is Osman Bey?

1290
02:02:45,310 --> 02:02:49,190
Neither me nor my alps!

1291
02:02:51,510 --> 02:02:53,580
We didn't do any of what you said.

1292
02:02:55,580 --> 02:03:00,080
Do not confuse us with you, you infidel!

1293
02:03:02,040 --> 02:03:03,750
Osman Bey will come.

1294
02:03:06,440 --> 02:03:10,750
Everyone will be waiting quietly until then.

1295
02:03:12,540 --> 02:03:15,570
The place where he will wait is not my tent.

1296
02:03:18,620 --> 02:03:21,610
If that's the case, we'll wait here.

1297
02:03:30,580 --> 02:03:32,630
Constantinople

1298
02:03:33,490 --> 02:03:36,310
I want dog Sarkis and Ophelia alive.

1299
02:03:36,910 --> 02:03:37,830
Run!

1300
02:04:19,420 --> 02:04:20,650
Sir Sarkis.

1301
02:04:21,110 --> 02:04:24,450
The emperor's men came to take princess.

1302
02:04:24,590 --> 02:04:25,910
They found us.

1303
02:04:26,500 --> 02:04:28,030
Don't worry princess.

1304
02:04:28,460 --> 02:04:29,920
We'll get you out of here.

1305
02:04:32,400 --> 02:04:33,480
Follow me.

1306
02:05:00,880 --> 02:05:03,060
It is clear that Osman Bey will not come.

1307
02:05:04,040 --> 02:05:05,250
Turgut Bey.

1308
02:05:05,620 --> 02:05:11,230
I ask you to hand me Oktem Bey
so that justice may be served.

1309
02:05:13,980 --> 02:05:17,580
Don't you hear?
We will wait for Osman Bey.

1310
02:05:20,400 --> 02:05:24,010
Nothing will be done before Osman Bey
comes, Kantakuzenos.

1311
02:05:24,590 --> 02:05:27,690
But Osman Bey promised me his life.

1312
02:05:28,430 --> 02:05:30,670
You will hand him over to me.

1313
02:05:31,300 --> 02:05:35,460
And I'll kill him in this tribe.

1314
02:05:54,760 --> 02:05:56,920
Hey freedom fighters!

1315
02:06:18,780 --> 02:06:22,040
You've come to the end of the road,
Princess Ophelia.

1316
02:06:26,750 --> 02:06:28,380
Slaves!

1317
02:06:32,070 --> 02:06:34,270
Give her to me.

1318
02:06:35,520 --> 02:06:39,800
I will never betray the emperor.

1319
02:06:41,530 --> 02:06:44,640
To whom do you raise your swords?

1320
02:06:45,120 --> 02:06:46,960
When my father heals...

1321
02:06:47,080 --> 02:06:50,100
You will all pay for this!

1322
02:07:07,580 --> 02:07:09,500
Princess Ophelia.

1323
02:07:10,880 --> 02:07:13,470
I came here to arrest you.

1324
02:07:14,280 --> 02:07:15,820
Who are you?

1325
02:07:16,080 --> 02:07:17,880
I am Olof.

1326
02:07:18,310 --> 02:07:21,320
Loyal leader of the emperor.

1327
02:07:23,580 --> 02:07:28,920
The rebellion started here,
with this traitor by your side.

1328
02:07:30,810 --> 02:07:33,230
And it will end where it began.

1329
02:07:50,200 --> 02:07:52,980
It's not over until I say it's over, Olof.

1330
02:07:54,560 --> 02:07:56,930
I don't know whom you serve to.

1331
02:07:57,770 --> 02:08:00,520
You won't take the princess
before you kill me.

1332
02:08:07,730 --> 02:08:09,840
Glad to hear that.

1333
02:09:58,840 --> 02:10:01,110
You will pay for all of this.

1334
02:10:09,450 --> 02:10:11,290
And it's today.

1335
02:10:20,030 --> 02:10:24,290
Whenever I point my axe at someone,
I find you in front of me, Osman!

1336
02:10:24,460 --> 02:10:27,090
Always point your axe
in the right direction.

1337
02:10:27,210 --> 02:10:31,450
You protected the guilty Oktem first,
and now you protect the traitor princess.

1338
02:10:31,600 --> 02:10:36,820
The walker of the right path
does not step back from any difficulty.

1339
02:10:48,310 --> 02:10:52,120
You killed my alps because of a slander!

1340
02:10:53,050 --> 02:10:55,490
You hid gold in my tribe.

1341
02:10:56,000 --> 02:10:58,890
You smeared my Beyship!

1342
02:10:59,640 --> 02:11:04,500
You came here and stopped me!

1343
02:11:05,670 --> 02:11:07,110
Alps.

1344
02:11:09,980 --> 02:11:18,870
And now you want my life in my tribe
in front of my people!

1345
02:11:27,100 --> 02:11:31,820
From now on,
my sword will secure the justice.

1346
02:11:31,940 --> 02:11:34,300
Alps! Alps!

1347
02:11:38,140 --> 02:11:39,770
Stop!

1348
02:11:40,030 --> 02:11:42,360
Why don't you hear listen to me?!

1349
02:11:52,340 --> 02:11:53,990
Alps!

1350
02:12:21,600 --> 02:12:22,940
Ophelia

1351
02:12:23,090 --> 02:12:25,150
They will take you, princess.

1352
02:12:31,110 --> 02:12:34,530
Catch her, don't let her escape!

1353
02:12:51,130 --> 02:12:54,140
She will go out, but you will stay.

1354
02:12:54,960 --> 02:12:57,330
If you stay, I will stay to kill you.

1355
02:12:57,520 --> 02:12:58,620
Come on then.

1356
02:12:58,790 --> 02:13:00,180
Come on.

1357
02:13:09,830 --> 02:13:12,080
It will end where it began.

1358
02:13:12,300 --> 02:13:16,530
Anyone who tries to stop us
is condemned to death.

1359
02:13:16,750 --> 02:13:19,220
My fire will burn you Osman.

1360
02:13:19,380 --> 02:13:23,140
I don't know to whom you serve.

1361
02:13:23,380 --> 02:13:25,800
But as long as I face you...

1362
02:13:26,300 --> 02:13:28,300
...I will end you one by one.

1363
02:13:42,719 --> 02:13:50,839
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com